<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="2CH" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">2 Chronicles</para>
  <para style="mt">2 Chronicles</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> the son of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was strengthened in his kingdom, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [was]</char> with him, and magnified him exceedingly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> spoke unto all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, to the captains of thousands and of hundreds, and to the judges, and to every governor in all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, the chief of the fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />So Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and all the congregation with him, went to the high place that <char style="add">[was]</char> at Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char>; for there was the tabernacle of the congregation of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> the servant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had made in the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But the ark of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> brought up from Kiryat-Ye’arim <char style="add">[City of Forests]</char> to <char style="add">[the place which]</char> David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had prepared for it: for he had pitched a tent for it at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Moreover the brasen altar, that B’tzal’el [In The Shadow <char style="pn">(Protection)</char> of El / God] the son of Uri <char style="add">[my light, my fire]</char>, the son of Hur <char style="add">[Liberty]</char>, had made, he put before the tabernacle of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> and the congregation sought unto it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> went up there to the brasen altar before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> at the tabernacle of the congregation, and offered a thousand burnt offerings upon it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />In that night did God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> appear unto Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and said unto him, Ask what I shall give you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> said unto God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> have showed great mercy unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father, and have made me to reign in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Now, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, let you<char style="ord">i</char> promise unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father be established: for you<char style="ord">i</char> have made me king over a people like the dust of the earth in multitude.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Give me now wisdom and knowledge, that I may go out and come in before this people: for who can judge this your<char style="ord">i</char> people, <char style="add">[that is so]</char> great?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> said to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, Because this was in you<char style="ord">i</char> heart, and you<char style="ord">i</char> have not asked riches, wealth, or honour, nor the life of you<char style="ord">i</char> enemies, neither yet have asked long life; but have asked wisdom and knowledge for yourself, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may judge my people, over whom I have made you<char style="ord">i</char> king:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Wisdom and knowledge <char style="add">[is]</char> granted unto you<char style="ord">i</char>; and I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> riches, and wealth, and honour, such as none of the kings have had that <char style="add">[have been]</char> before you<char style="ord">i</char>, neither shall there any after you<char style="ord">i</char> have the like.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Then Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> came <char style="add">[from his journey]</char> to the high place that <char style="add">[was]</char> at Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char> to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, from before the tabernacle of the congregation, and reigned over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> gathered chariots and horsemen: and he had a thousand and four hundred chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen, which he placed in the chariot cities, and with the king at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the king made silver and gold at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace] [as plenteous]</char> as stones, and cedar trees made he as the sycomore trees that <char style="add">[are]</char> in the vale for abundance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had horses brought out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and linen yarn: the king’s merchants received the linen yarn at a price.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And they fetched up, and brought forth out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> a chariot for six hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of silver, and an horse for an hundred and fifty: and so brought they out <char style="add">[horses]</char> for all the kings of the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and for the kings of Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, by their means.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> determined to build an house for the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and an house for his kingdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> tallied threescore and ten thousand men to bear burdens, and eighty thousand to hew in the mountain, and three thousand and six hundred to oversee them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> sent to Huram <char style="add">[noble born]</char> the king of Tzor <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, saying, As you<char style="ord">i</char> did deal with David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father, and did send him cedars to build him an house to dwell in it, <char style="add">[even so deal with me]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Behold, I build an house to the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, to dedicate <char style="add">[it]</char> to him, <char style="add">[and]</char> to burn before him sweet incense, and for the continual showbread, and for the burnt offerings morning and evening, on the Shabbat, and on the new moons, and on the solemn feasts of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. This <char style="add">[is an ordinance]</char> forever to Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the house which I build <char style="add">[is]</char> great: for great <char style="add">[is]</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> above all gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But who is able to build him an house, seeing the heaven and heaven of heavens cannot contain him? who <char style="add">[am]</char> I then, that I should build him an house, save only to burn sacrifice before him?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Send me now therefore a man cunning to work in gold, and in silver, and in brass, and in iron, and in purple, and crimson, and blue, and that can skill to grave with the cunning men that <char style="add">[are]</char> with me in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, whom David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father did provide.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Send me also cedar trees, fir trees, and algum trees, out of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>: for I know that you<char style="ord">i</char> servants can skill to cut timber in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>; and, behold, my servants <char style="add">[shall be]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char> servants,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Even to prepare me timber in abundance: for the house which I am about to build <char style="add">[shall be]</char> wonderful great.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And, behold, I will give to you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, the hewers that cut timber, twenty thousand measures of beaten wheat, and twenty thousand measures of barley, and twenty thousand baths of wine, and twenty thousand baths of oil.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then Huram <char style="add">[noble born]</char> the king of Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyre)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char> answered in writing, which he sent to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, Because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has loved his people, he has made you<char style="ord">i</char> king over them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Huram <char style="add">[noble born]</char> said moreover, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that made heaven and earth, who has given to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> the king a wise son, endued with prudence and understanding, that might build an house for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and an house for his kingdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And now I have sent a cunning man, endued with understanding, of Huram <char style="add">[noble born]</char> my father’s,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />The son of a woman of the daughters of Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, and his father <char style="add">[was]</char> a man of Tzor <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, skilful to work in gold, and in silver, in brass, in iron, in stone, and in timber, in purple, in blue, and in fine linen, and in crimson; also to grave any manner of graving, and to find out every device which shall be put to him, with you<char style="ord">i</char> cunning men, and with the cunning men of my lord David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Now therefore the wheat, and the barley, the oil, and the wine, which my lord has spoken of, let him send unto his servants:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And we will cut wood out of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, as much as you<char style="ord">i</char> shall need: and we will bring it to you<char style="ord">i</char> in floats by sea to Joppa; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall carry it up to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> numbered all the strangers that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, after the numbering which David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father had numbered them; and they were found an hundred and fifty thousand and three thousand and six hundred.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he set threescore and ten thousand of them <char style="add">[to be]</char> bearers of burdens, and eighty thousand <char style="add">[to be]</char> hewers in the mountain, and three thousand and six hundred overseers to set the people a work.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> began to build the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> in Mount Moriyah <char style="add">[chosen by Yehovah]</char>, where <char style="add">[the LORD-Yehōvah (Messiah Pre-Incarnate)]</char> appeared unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father, in the place that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had prepared in the threshingfloor of Ornan <char style="add">[light was perpetuated]</char> the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he began to build in the second <char style="add">[day]</char> of the second month, in the fourth year of his reign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now these <char style="add">[are the things wherein]</char> Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> was instructed for the building of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. The length by cubits after the first measure <char style="add">[was]</char> threescore cubits, and the breadth twenty cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the porch that <char style="add">[was]</char> in the front <char style="add">[of the house]</char>, the length <char style="add">[of it was]</char> according to the breadth of the house, twenty cubits, and the height <char style="add">[was]</char> an hundred and twenty: and he overlaid it within with pure gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the greater house he ceilinged with fir tree, which he overlaid with fine gold, and set thereon palm trees and chains.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he garnished the house with precious stones for beauty: and the gold <char style="add">[was]</char> gold of Parayim <char style="add">[oriental regions]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />He overlaid also the house, the beams, the posts, and the walls thereof, and the doors thereof, with gold; and graved k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> on the walls.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he made the most holy house, the length whereof <char style="add">[was]</char> according to the breadth of the house, twenty cubits, and the breadth thereof twenty cubits: and he overlaid it with fine gold, <char style="add">[amounting]</char> to six hundred talents.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the weight of the nails <char style="add">[was]</char> fifty shekels of gold. And he overlaid the upper chambers with gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And in the most holy house he made two k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> of image work, and overlaid them with gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the wings of the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> <char style="add">[were]</char> twenty cubits long: one wing [of the one cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char> was] five cubits, reaching to the wall of the house: and the other wing <char style="add">[was likewise]</char> five cubits, reaching to the wing of the other cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And <char style="add">[one]</char> wing of the other cherub <char style="add">[keruv] [was]</char> five cubits, reaching to the wall of the house: and the other wing <char style="add">[was]</char> five cubits <char style="add">[also]</char>, joining to the wing of the other cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />The wings of these k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> spread themselves forth twenty cubits: and they stood on their feet, and their faces <char style="add">[were]</char> inward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he made the vail <char style="add">[of]</char> blue, and purple, and crimson, and fine linen, and wrought k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> thereon.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Also he made before the house two pillars of thirty and five cubits high, and the column that <char style="add">[was]</char> on the top of each of them <char style="add">[was]</char> five cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he made chains, <char style="add">[as]</char> in the oracle, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> on the heads of the pillars; and made an hundred pomegranates, and put <char style="add">[them]</char> on the chains.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he reared up the pillars before the temple, one on the right hand, and the other on the left; and called the name of that on the right hand Yakhin <char style="add">[He will establish]</char>, and the name of that on the left Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Moreover he made an altar of brass, twenty cubits the length thereof, and twenty cubits the breadth thereof, and ten cubits the height thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Also he made a molten sea of ten cubits from brim to brim, round in compass (go around, encircle; encompass), and five cubits the height thereof; and a line of thirty cubits did compass <char style="pn">(go around, encircle; encompass)</char> it round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And under it <char style="add">[was]</char> the similitude of oxen, which did compass <char style="pn">(go around, encircle; encompass)</char> it round about: ten in a cubit, compassing the sea round about. Two rows of oxen <char style="add">[were]</char> cast, when it was cast.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />It stood upon twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, and three looking toward the west, and three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east: and the sea <char style="add">[was set]</char> above upon them, and all their hinder parts <char style="add">[were]</char> inward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the thickness of it <char style="add">[was]</char> an handbreadth, and the brim of it like the work of the brim of a cup, with flowers of lilies; <char style="add">[and]</char> it received and held three thousand baths.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />He made also ten lavers, and put five on the right hand, and five on the left, to wash in them: such things as they offered for the burnt offering they washed in them; but the sea <char style="add">[was]</char> for the priests to wash in.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he made ten candlesticks of gold according to their form, and set <char style="add">[them]</char> in the temple, five on the right hand, and five on the left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />He made also ten tables, and placed <char style="add">[them]</char> in the temple, five on the right side, and five on the left. And he made an hundred basons of gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Furthermore he made the court of the priests, and the great court, and doors for the court, and overlaid the doors of them with brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he set the sea on the right side of the east end, over against the south.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Huram <char style="add">[noble born]</char> made the pots, and the shovels, and the basons. And Huram <char style="add">[noble born]</char> finished the work that he was to make for king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> for the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[To wit]</char>, the two pillars, and the pommels <char style="pn">(bowl-shaped top of a pillar)</char>, and the columns <char style="add">[which were]</char> on the top of the two pillars, and the two wreaths to cover the two pommels <char style="pn">(bowl-shaped top of a pillar)</char> of the columns which <char style="add">[were]</char> on the top of the pillars;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And four hundred pomegranates on the two wreaths; two rows of pomegranates on each wreath, to cover the two pommels <char style="pn">(bowl-shaped top of a pillar)</char> of the columns which <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the pillars.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />He made also bases, and lavers made he upon the bases;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />One sea, and twelve oxen under it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />The pots also, and the shovels, and the fleshhooks, and all their instruments, did Huram <char style="add">[noble born]</char> his father make to king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> for the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> of bright brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />In the plain of Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> did the king cast them, in the clay ground between Sukkot <char style="add">[Booths]</char> and Tz’redah <char style="add">[fortress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Thus Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> made all these vessels in great abundance: for the weight of the brass could not be found out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> made all the vessels that <char style="add">[were for]</char> the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, the golden altar also, and the tables whereon the showbread <char style="add">[was set]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Moreover the candlesticks with their lamps, that they should burn after the manner before the oracle, of pure gold;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the flowers, and the lamps, and the tongs, <char style="add">[made he of]</char> gold, <char style="add">[and]</char> that perfect gold;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the snuffers, and the basons, and the spoons, and the censers, <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold: and the entry of the house, the inner doors thereof for the most holy <char style="add">[place]</char>, and the doors of the house of the temple, <char style="add">[were of]</char> gold.</para>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Thus all the work that Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> made for the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was finished: and Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> brought in <char style="add">[all]</char> the things that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father had dedicated; and the silver, and the gold, and all the instruments, put he among the treasures of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> assembled the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and all the heads of the tribes, the chief of the fathers of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, unto Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, to bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> out of the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />For what reason all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> assembled themselves unto the king in the feast which <char style="add">[was]</char> in the seventh month.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And all the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came; and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> took up the ark.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And they brought up the ark, and the tabernacle of the congregation, and all the holy vessels that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the tabernacle, these did the priests <char style="add">[and]</char> the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> bring up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Also king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and all the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that were assembled unto him before the ark, sacrificed sheep and oxen, which could not be told nor numbered for multitude.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the priests brought in the ark of the covenant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto his place, to the oracle of the house, into the most holy <char style="add">[place, even]</char> under the wings of the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />For the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> spread forth <char style="add">[their]</char> wings over the place of the ark, and the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> covered the ark and the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> thereof above.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And they drew out the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> <char style="add">[of the ark]</char>, that the ends of the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> were seen from the ark before the oracle; but they were not seen without. And there it is unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[There was]</char> nothing in the ark save the two tables which Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> put <char style="add">[in it]</char> at Horev <char style="add">[Desert]</char>, when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> made <char style="add">[a covenant]</char> with the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when they came out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the priests were come out of the holy <char style="add">[place]</char> (for all the priests <char style="add">[that were]</char> present were sanctified, <char style="add">[and]</char> did not <char style="add">[then]</char> wait by course):</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Also the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to] [which were]</char> the singers, all of them of Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char>, of Heiman <char style="add">[faithful]</char>, of Y’dutun <char style="add">[praising]</char>, with their sons and their brethren, <char style="add">[being]</char> arrayed in white linen, having cymbals and psalteries and harps, stood at the east end of the altar, and with them an hundred and twenty priests sounding with trumpets</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />It came even to pass, as the trumpeters and singers <char style="add">[were]</char> as one, to make one sound to be heard in praising and thanking the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and when they lifted up <char style="add">[their]</char> voice with the trumpets and cymbals and instruments of music, and praised the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, For <char style="add">[he is]</char> good; for his mercy <char style="add">[endures]</char> forever: that <char style="add">[then]</char> the house was filled with a cloud, <char style="add">[even]</char> the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />So that the priests could not stand to minister by reason of the cloud: for the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had filled the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then said Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has said that he would dwell in the thick darkness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />But I have built an house of habitation for you<char style="ord">i</char>, and a place for you<char style="ord">i</char> dwelling forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the king turned his face, and Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> the whole congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and all the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> stood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he said, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, who has with his hands fulfilled <char style="add">[that]</char> which he spoke with his mouth to my father David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Since the day that I brought forth my people out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> I chose no city among all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to build an house in, that my name might be there; neither chose I any man to be a ruler over my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But I have chosen Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, that my name might be there; and have chosen David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to be over my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Now it was in the heart of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father to build an house for the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father, Forasmuch as it was in you<char style="ord">i</char> heart to build an house for my name, you<char style="ord">i</char> did well in that it was in you<char style="ord">i</char> heart:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Yet you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not build the house; but you<char style="ord">i</char> son which shall come forth out of you<char style="ord">i</char> waist, he shall build the house for my name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> therefore has performed his word that he has spoken: for I am risen up in the room of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father, and am set on the throne of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> promised, and have built the house for the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And in it have I put the ark, wherein <char style="add">[is]</char> the covenant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that he made with the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he stood before the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in the presence of all the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and spread forth his hands:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />For Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had made a brasen scaffold, of five cubits long, and five cubits broad, and three cubits high, and had set it in the midst of the court: and upon it he stood, and kneeled down upon his knees before all the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and spread forth his hands toward heaven,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And said, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[there is]</char> no God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> like you<char style="ord">i</char> in the heaven, nor in the earth; which keeps covenant, and <char style="add">[shows]</char> mercy unto you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, that walk before you<char style="ord">i</char> with all their hearts:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> which have kept with your<char style="ord">i</char> servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father that which you<char style="ord">i</char> have promised him; and spoke with your<char style="ord">i</char> mouth, and have fulfilled <char style="add">[it]</char> with your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, as <char style="add">[it is]</char> this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Now therefore, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, keep with you<char style="ord">i</char> servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father that which you<char style="ord">i</char> have promised him, saying, There shall not fail you<char style="ord">i</char> a man in my sight to sit upon the throne of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; yet so that your<char style="ord">i</char> children take heed to their way to walk in my law, as you<char style="ord">i</char> have walked before me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Now then, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, let your<char style="ord">i</char> word be verified, which you<char style="ord">i</char> have spoken unto your<char style="ord">i</char> servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />But will God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in very deed dwell with men on the earth? behold, heaven and the heaven of heavens cannot contain you<char style="ord">i</char>; how much less this house which I have built!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Have respect therefore to the prayer of your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, and to his supplication, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, to hearken unto the cry and the prayer which your<char style="ord">i</char> servant prays before you<char style="ord">i</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />That your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes may be open upon this house day and night, upon the place whereof you<char style="ord">i</char> have said that you<char style="ord">i</char> would put your<char style="ord">i</char> name there; to hearken unto the prayer which your<char style="ord">i</char> servant prays toward this place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Listen therefore unto the supplications of your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, and of your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which they shall make toward this place: hear you<char style="ord">i</char> from your<char style="ord">i</char> dwelling place, <char style="add">[even]</char> from heaven; and when you<char style="ord">i</char> hear, forgive.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />If a man sin against his neighbour, and an oath be laid upon him to make him swear, and the oath come before your<char style="ord">i</char> altar in this house;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> from heaven, and do, and judge your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, by requiting the wicked, by recompensing his way upon his own head; and by justifying the righteous, by giving him according to his righteousness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And if your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> be put to the worse before the enemy, because they have sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char>; and shall return and confess your<char style="ord">i</char> name, and pray and make supplication before you<char style="ord">i</char> in this house;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> from the heavens, and forgive the sin of your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and bring them again unto the land which you<char style="ord">i</char> gave to them and to their fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />When the heaven is shut up, and there is no rain, because they have sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char>; <char style="add">[yet]</char> if they pray toward this place, and confess your<char style="ord">i</char> name, and turn from their sin, when you<char style="ord">i</char> do afflict them;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> from heaven, and forgive the sin of your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and of your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when you<char style="ord">i</char> have taught them the good way, wherein they should walk; and send rain upon you<char style="ord">i</char> land, which you<char style="ord">i</char> have given unto your<char style="ord">i</char> people for an inheritance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />If there be famine in the land, if there be pestilence, if there be blasting, or mildew, locusts, or caterpillers; if their enemies besiege them in the cities of their land; whatsoever sore or whatsoever sickness <char style="add">[there be]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Then]</char> what prayer <char style="add">[or]</char> what supplication whatsoever shall be made of any man, or of all you<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when every one shall know his own sore and his own grief, and shall spread forth his hands in this house:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> from heaven your<char style="ord">i</char> dwelling place, and forgive, and render unto every man according unto all his ways, whose heart you<char style="ord">i</char> know; (for you<char style="ord">i</char> only know the hearts of the children of men)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />That they may fear you<char style="ord">i</char>, to walk in your<char style="ord">i</char> ways, so long as they live in the land which you<char style="ord">i</char> gave unto our fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Moreover concerning the stranger, which is not of your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, but is come from a far country for your<char style="ord">i</char> great name’s sake, and your<char style="ord">i</char> mighty hand, and your<char style="ord">i</char> stretched out arm; if they come and pray in this house;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> from the heavens, <char style="add">[even]</char> from your<char style="ord">i</char> dwelling place, and do according to all that the stranger calls to you<char style="ord">i</char> for; that all people of the earth may know your<char style="ord">i</char> name, and fear you<char style="ord">i</char>, as <char style="add">[does]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and may know that this house which I have built is called by your<char style="ord">i</char> name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />If you<char style="ord">i</char> people go out to war against their enemies by the way that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall send them, and they pray unto you<char style="ord">i</char> toward this city which you<char style="ord">i</char> have chosen, and the house which I have built for your<char style="ord">i</char> name;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> from the heavens their prayer and their supplication, and maintain their cause.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />If they sin against you<char style="ord">i</char>, (for <char style="add">[there is]</char> no man which sins not,) and you<char style="ord">i</char> be angry with them, and deliver them over before <char style="add">[their]</char> enemies, and they carry them away captives unto a land far off or near;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Yet <char style="add">[if]</char> they reconsider themselves in the land to which they are carried captive, and turn and pray unto you<char style="ord">i</char> in the land of their captivity, saying, We have sinned, we have done amiss <char style="pn">(wrong; incorrect)</char>, and have dealt wickedly;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />If they return to you<char style="ord">i</char> with all their heart and with all their soul in the land of their captivity, to which they have carried them captives, and pray toward their land, which you<char style="ord">i</char> gave unto their fathers, and <char style="add">[toward]</char> the city which you<char style="ord">i</char> have chosen, and toward the house which I have built for your<char style="ord">i</char> name:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> from the heavens, <char style="add">[even]</char> from your<char style="ord">i</char> dwelling place, their prayer and their supplications, and maintain their cause, and forgive your<char style="ord">i</char> people which have sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />Now, my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, let, I beseech <char style="pn">(to call upon; appeal; beg)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes be open, and <char style="add">[let]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> ears <char style="add">[be]</char> attentive unto the prayer <char style="add">[that is made]</char> in this place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />Now therefore arise, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, into your<char style="ord">i</char> resting place, you<char style="ord">i</char>, and the ark of your<char style="ord">i</char> strength: let your<char style="ord">i</char> priests, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, be clothed with salvation, and let you<char style="ord">i</char> saints rejoice in goodness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, turn not away the face of you<char style="ord">i</char> anointed: remember the mercies of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> servant.</para>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now when Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had made an end of praying, the fire came down from heaven, and consumed the burnt offering and the sacrifices; and the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> filled the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the priests could not enter into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, because the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had filled the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And when all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> saw how the fire came down, and the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> upon the house, they bowed themselves with their faces to the ground upon the pavement, and worshipped, and praised the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, For <char style="add">[he is]</char> good; for his mercy <char style="add">[endures]</char> forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Then the king and all the people offered sacrifices before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> offered a sacrifice of twenty and two thousand oxen, and an hundred and twenty thousand sheep: so the king and all the people dedicated the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the priests waited on their offices: the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> also with instruments of music of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> the king had made to praise the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, because his mercy <char style="add">[endures]</char> forever, when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> praised by their ministry; and the priests sounded trumpets before them, and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> stood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Moreover Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> consecrated the middle of the court that <char style="add">[was]</char> before the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for there he offered burnt offerings, and the fat of the peace offerings, because the brasen altar which Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had made was not able to receive the burnt offerings, and the meat offerings, and the fat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Also at the same time Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> kept the feast seven days, and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with him, a very great congregation, from the entering in of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char> unto the river of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And in the eighth day they made a solemn assembly: for they kept the dedication of the altar seven days, and the feast seven days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And on the three and twentieth day of the seventh month he sent the people away into their tents, glad and merry in heart for the goodness that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had showed unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and to Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> his people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Thus Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> finished the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the king’s house: and all that came into Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> heart to make in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and in his own house, he prosperously effected.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> appeared to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> by night, and said unto him, I have heard you<char style="ord">i</char> prayer, and have chosen this place to myself for an house of sacrifice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />If I shut up heaven that there be no rain, or if I command the locusts to devour the land, or if I send pestilence among my people;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />If my people, which are called by my name, shall humble themselves, and pray, and seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways; then will I hear from heaven, and will forgive their sin, and will heal their land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Now my eyes shall be open, and my ears attentive unto the prayer <char style="add">[that is made]</char> in this place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />For now have I chosen and sanctified this house, that my name may be there forever: and my eyes and my heart shall be there perpetually.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And as for you<char style="ord">i</char>, if you<char style="ord">i</char> will walk before me, as David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> father walked, and do according to all that I have commanded you<char style="ord">i</char>, and shall observe my statutes and my judgments;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then will I establish the throne of your<char style="ord">i</char> kingdom, according as I have covenanted with David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> father, saying, There shall not fail you<char style="ord">i</char> a man <char style="add">[to be]</char> ruler in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />But if you<char style="ord">2f</char> turn away, and forsake my statutes and my commandments, which I have set before you, and shall go and serve other gods, and worship them;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then will I pluck them up by the roots out of my land which I have given them; and this house, which I have sanctified for my name, will I cast out of my sight, and will make it <char style="add">[to be]</char> a proverb and a byword among all nations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And this house, which is high, shall be an astonishment to every one that passes by it; so that he shall say, Why has the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> done thus unto this land, and unto this house?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And it shall be answered, Because they forsook the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers, which brought them forth out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and laid hold on other gods, and worshipped them, and served them: therefore has he brought all this evil upon them.</para>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass at the end of twenty years, wherein Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had built the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and his own house,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />That the cities which Huram <char style="add">[noble born]</char> had restored to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> built them, and caused the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to dwell there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> went to Hamat-Tzovah <char style="add">[fortress of station]</char>, and prevailed against it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he built Tadmor <char style="add">[palm tree]</char> in the wilderness, and all the store cities, which he built in Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Also he built Beit-Horon <char style="add">[House of Hollowness]</char> the upper, and Beit-Horon <char style="add">[House of Hollowness]</char> the lower, fenced cities, with walls, gates, and bars;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Ba’alat <char style="add">[mistress]</char>, and all the store cities that Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had, and all the chariot cities, and the cities of the horsemen, and all that Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> desired to build in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, and throughout all the land of his dominion.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[As for]</char> all the people <char style="add">[that were]</char> left of the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, and the P’rizi <char style="add">[Dwellers in Unwalled Towns]</char>, and the Hivi <char style="add">[Villagers]</char>, and the Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char>, which <char style="add">[were]</char> not of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[But]</char> of their children, who were left after them in the land, whom the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> consumed not, them did Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> make to pay tribute until this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> make no servants for his work; but they <char style="add">[were]</char> men of war, and chief of his captains, and captains of his chariots and horsemen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[were]</char> the chief of king Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> officers, <char style="add">[even]</char> two hundred and fifty, that bore rule over the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> brought up the daughter of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> out of the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> unto the house that he had built for her: for he said, My wife shall not dwell in the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, because <char style="add">[the places are]</char> holy, whereunto the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has come.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> offered burnt offerings unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> on the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he had built before the porch,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Even after a certain rate every day, offering according to the commandment of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, on the Shabbat, and on the new moons, and on the solemn feasts, three times in the year, <char style="add">[even]</char> in the feast of unleavened bread, and in the feast of weeks, and in the feast of tabernacles.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he appointed, according to the order of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father, the courses of the priests to their service, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> to their charges, to praise and minister before the priests, as the duty of every day required: the porters also by their courses at every gate: for so had David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> commanded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And they departed not from the commandment of the king unto the priests and Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> concerning any matter, or concerning the treasures.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Now all the work of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> was prepared unto the day of the foundation of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and until it was finished. <char style="add">[So]</char> the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was perfected.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then went Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> to ‘Etzyon-Gever <char style="add">[backbone of a man]</char>, and to Elot <char style="add">[grove of lofty trees]</char>, at the sea side in the land of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Huram <char style="add">[noble born]</char> sent him by the hands of his servants ships, and servants that had knowledge of the sea; and they went with the servants of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> to Ofir <char style="add">[reducing to ashes]</char>, and took there four hundred and fifty talents of gold, and brought <char style="add">[them]</char> to king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And when the Queen of Sh’va <char style="add">[seven, an oath]</char> heard of the fame of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, she came to prove Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> with hard questions at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, with a very great company, and camels that bore spices, and gold in abundance, and precious stones: and when she was come to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, she communed with him of all that was in her heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> told her all her questions: and there was nothing hid from Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> which he told her not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And when the Queen of Sh’va <char style="add">[seven, an oath]</char> had seen the wisdom of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and the house that he had built,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the meat of his table, and the sitting of his servants, and the attendance of his ministers, and their apparel; his cupbearers also, and their apparel; and his ascent by which he went up into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; there was no more spirit in her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And she said to the king, <char style="add">[It was]</char> a true report which I heard in my own land of you<char style="ord">i</char> acts, and of you<char style="ord">i</char> wisdom:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />However I believed not their words, until I came, and my eyes had seen <char style="add">[it]</char>: and, behold, the one half of the greatness of you<char style="ord">i</char> wisdom was not told me: <char style="add">[for]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> exceed the fame that I heard.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Happy <char style="add">[are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> men, and happy <char style="add">[are]</char> these you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, which stand continually before you<char style="ord">i</char>, and hear you<char style="ord">i</char> wisdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> be the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which delighted in you<char style="ord">i</char> to set you<char style="ord">i</char> on his throne, <char style="add">[to be]</char> king for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: because you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> loved Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, to establish them forever, therefore made he you<char style="ord">i</char> king over them, to do judgment and justice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And she gave the king an hundred and twenty talents of gold, and of spices great abundance, and precious stones: neither was there any such spice as the Queen of Sh’va <char style="add">[seven, an oath]</char> gave king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the servants also of Huram <char style="add">[noble born]</char>, and the servants of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, which brought gold from Ofir <char style="add">[reducing to ashes]</char>, brought algum trees and precious stones.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the king made <char style="add">[of]</char> the algum trees terraces to the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and to the king’s palace, and harps and psalteries for singers: and there were none such seen before in the land of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> gave to the Queen of Sh’va <char style="add">[seven, an oath]</char> all her desire, whatsoever she asked, beside <char style="add">[that]</char> which she had brought unto the king. So she turned, and went away to her own land, she and her servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Now the weight of gold that came to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> in one year was six hundred and threescore and six talents of gold;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Beside <char style="add">[that which]</char> merchants and merchants brought. And all the kings of Arabia <char style="add">[steppe-dwellers]</char> and governors of the country brought gold and silver to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> made two hundred targets <char style="add">[of]</char> beaten gold: six hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of beaten gold went to one target <char style="pn">(small shield; buckler)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And three hundred shields <char style="add">[made he of]</char> beaten gold: three hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of gold went to one shield. And the king put them in the house of the forest of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Moreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with pure gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there were]</char> six steps to the throne, with a footstool of gold, <char style="add">[which were]</char> fastened to the throne, and stays on each side of the sitting place, and two lions standing by the stays:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other upon the six steps. There was not the like made in any kingdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And all the drinking vessels of king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace] [were of]</char> gold, and all the vessels of the house of the forest of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness] [were of]</char> pure gold: none <char style="add">[were of]</char> silver; it was <char style="add">[not]</char> any thing accounted of in the days of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />For the king’s ships went to Tarshish <char style="add">[yellow jasper]</char> with the servants of Huram <char style="add">[noble born]</char>: every three years once came the ships of Tarshish <char style="add">[yellow jasper]</char> bringing gold, and silver, ivory, and apes, and peacocks.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> passed all the kings of the earth in riches and wisdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And all the kings of the earth sought the presence of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, to hear his wisdom, that God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had put in his heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And they brought every man his present, vessels of silver, and vessels of gold, and clothing, harness, and spices, horses, and mules, a rate year by year.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had four thousand stalls for horses and chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen; whom he bestowed in the chariot cities, and with the king at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And he reigned over all the kings from the river even unto the land of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and to the border of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the king made silver in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> as stones, and cedar trees made he as the sycomore trees that <char style="add">[are]</char> in the low plains in abundance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And they brought unto Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> horses out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and out of all lands.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, first and last, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet, and in the prophecy of Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char> the Shiloni <char style="add">[peace bringer] [place of rest]</char>, and in the visions of ‘Iddo <char style="add">[His witness]</char> the seer against Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> reigned in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> over all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> forty years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> slept with his fathers, and he was buried in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father: and Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> went to Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>: for to Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> were all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> come to make him king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, who <char style="add">[was]</char> in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, to which he had fled from the presence of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> the king, heard <char style="add">[it]</char>, that Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> returned out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And they sent and called him. So Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came and spoke to Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />You<char style="ord">1s</char> father made our yoke grievous: now therefore ease you<char style="ord">i</char> somewhat the grievous servitude of your<char style="ord">i</char> father, and his heavy yoke that he put upon us, and we will serve you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he said unto them, Come again unto me after three days. And the people departed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> took counsel with the old men that had stood before Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> his father while he yet lived, saying, What counsel give you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[me]</char> to return answer to this people?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And they spoke unto him, saying, If you<char style="ord">i</char> be kind to this people, and please them, and speak good words to them, they will be your<char style="ord">i</char> servants forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But he forsook the counsel which the old men gave him, and took counsel with the young men that were brought up with him, that stood before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he said unto them, What advice give you<char style="ord">2f</char> that we may return answer to this people, which have spoken to me, saying, Ease somewhat the yoke that you<char style="ord">i</char> father did put upon us?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the young men that were brought up with him spoke unto him, saying, Thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> answer the people that spoke unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, You<char style="ord">1s</char> father made our yoke heavy, but make you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[it]</char> somewhat lighter for us; thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> say unto them, My little <char style="add">[finger]</char> shall be thicker than my father’s waist.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For whereas my father put a heavy yoke upon you, I will put more to your yoke: my father chastised you with whips, but I <char style="add">[will chastise you]</char> with scorpions.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />So Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> and all the people came to Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> on the third day, as the king bade, saying, Come again to me on the third day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the king answered them roughly; and king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> forsook the counsel of the old men,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And answered them after the advice of the young men, saying, My father made your yoke heavy, but I will add thereto: my father chastised you with whips, but I <char style="add">[will chastise you]</char> with scorpions.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />So the king listened not unto the people: for the cause was of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> might perform his word, which he spoke by the hand of Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char> the Shiloni <char style="add">[peace bringer] [place of rest]</char> to Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And when all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [saw]</char> that the king would not hearken unto them, the people answered the king, saying, What portion have we in David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>? and <char style="add">[we have]</char> none inheritance in the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>: every man to your tents, O Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: <char style="add">[and]</char> now, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, see to you<char style="ord">i</char> own house. So all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went to their tents.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />But <char style="add">[as for]</char> the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that dwelt in the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> reigned over them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> sent Hadoram <char style="add">[noble honour]</char> that <char style="add">[was]</char> over the tribute; and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> stoned him with stones, that he died. But king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> made speed to get him up to <char style="add">[his]</char> chariot, to flee to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> rebelled against the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> unto this day.</para>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And when Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> was come to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, he gathered of the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> an hundred and eighty thousand chosen <char style="add">[men]</char>, which were warriors, to fight against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that he might bring the kingdom again to Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />But the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came to Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char> the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Speak unto Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> the son of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and to all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not go up, nor fight against your brethren: return every man to his house: for this thing is done of me. And they obeyed the words of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and returned from going against Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> dwelt in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and built cities for defence in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />He built even Beit-Lechem <char style="add">[House of Bread]</char>, and ‘Eitam <char style="add">[Lair of Wild Beasts]</char>, and T’koa <char style="add">[a stockade]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Beit’Tzur <char style="add">[House of the Rock]</char>, and Sokho <char style="add">[bushy]</char>, and ‘Adulam <char style="add">[Justice of the People]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, and Mareshah <char style="add">[Crest of a Hill]</char>, and Ziv <char style="add">[brightness]</char> [Battlement (low wall around a roof; wall for defense)],</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Adorayim <char style="add">[double glory]</char>, and Lakhish <char style="add">[Invincible]</char>, and ‘Azekah <char style="add">[Dug Over]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Tzor’ah <char style="add">[Hornet]</char>, and Ayalon <char style="add">[Field of Deer]</char>, and Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>, which <char style="add">[are]</char> in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and in Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> fenced cities.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he fortified the strong holds, and put captains in them, and store of victual, and of oil and wine.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And in every single <char style="pn">(each one separately)</char> city <char style="add">[he put]</char> shields and spears, and made them exceeding strong, having Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> on his side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> that <char style="add">[were]</char> in all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> resorted to him out of all their coasts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />For the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> left their suburbs and their possession, and came to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: for Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> and his sons had cast them off from executing the priest’s office unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he ordained him priests for the high places, and for the devils, and for the calves which he had made.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And after them out of all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> such as set their hearts to seek the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, to sacrifice unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />So they strengthened the kingdom of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and made Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> the son of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> strong, three years: for three years they walked in the way of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> took him Mahalath the daughter of Yerimot <char style="add">[He is Most High]</char> the son of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to wife, <char style="add">[and]</char> Avichayil <char style="add">[Father of Strength]</char> the daughter of ‘Eli’av <char style="add">[My Father is God]</char> the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Which bore him children; Ye’ush <char style="add">[He hurries to aid]</char>, and Sh’maryah <char style="add">[kept by Yehovah]</char>, and Zaham <char style="add">[loathing]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And after her he took Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression]</char> the daughter of Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>; which bore him Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char>, and ‘Atai <char style="add">[opportune]</char>, and Ziza <char style="add">[shining]</char>, and Shlomit <char style="add">[Peaceful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> loved Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression]</char> the daughter of Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> above all his wives and his concubines (for he took eighteen wives, and threescore concubines; and begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> twenty and eight sons, and threescore daughters.)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> made Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> the son of Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression]</char> the chief, <char style="add">[to be]</char> ruler among his brethren: for <char style="add">[he thought]</char> to make him king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he dealt wisely, and dispersed of all his children throughout all the countries of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, unto every fenced city: and he gave them victual in abundance. And he desired many wives.</para>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> had established the kingdom, and had strengthened himself, he forsook the law of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And it came to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> in the fifth year of king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> Shishak <char style="add">[greedy of fine linen]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> came up against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, because they had transgressed against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />With twelve hundred chariots, and threescore thousand horsemen: and the people <char style="add">[were]</char> without number that came with him out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>; the Luvim <char style="add">[empty-hearted]</char>, the Suki’im <char style="add">[booth dwellers]</char>, and the Cushi <char style="add">[Ethiopians]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he took the fenced cities which <char style="add">[pertained]</char> to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then came Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char> the prophet to Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char>, and <char style="add">[to]</char> the princes of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, that were gathered together to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> because of Shishak <char style="add">[greedy of fine linen]</char>, and said unto them, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, You<char style="ord">2f</char> have forsaken me, and therefore have I also left you in the hand of Shishak <char style="add">[greedy of fine linen]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Whereupon the princes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and the king humbled themselves; and they said, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> righteous.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> saw that they humbled themselves, the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came to Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>, saying, They have humbled themselves; <char style="add">[therefore]</char> I will not destroy them, but I will grant them some deliverance; and my wrath shall not be poured out upon Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> by the hand of Shishak <char style="add">[greedy of fine linen]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Nevertheless they shall be his servants; that they may know my service, and the service of the kingdoms of the countries.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />So Shishak <char style="add">[greedy of fine linen]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> came up against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and took away the treasures of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the treasures of the king’s house; he took all: he carried away also the shields of gold which Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had made.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Instead of which king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> made shields of brass, and committed <char style="add">[them]</char> to the hands of the chief of the guard, that kept the entrance of the king’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And when the king entered into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the guard came and fetched them, and brought them again into the guard chamber.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And when he humbled himself, the wrath of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> turned from him, that he would not destroy <char style="add">[him]</char> altogether: and also in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> things went well.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />So king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> strengthened himself in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and reigned: for Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged] [was]</char> one and forty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned seventeen years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, the city which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had chosen out of all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, to put his name there. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Na’amah <char style="add">[Loveliness]</char> an ‘Amonit <char style="add">[tribal]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he did evil, because he prepared not his heart to seek the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Now the acts of Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char>, first and last, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char> the prophet, and of ‘Iddo <char style="add">[His witness]</char> the seer concerning genealogies? And <char style="add">[there were]</char> wars between Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> and Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> continually.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now in the eighteenth year of king Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> began Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> to reign over Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />He reigned three years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. His mother’s name also <char style="add">[was]</char> Mikhayah <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> the daughter of Uri’el <char style="add">[God is my light]</char> of Giv’ah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>. And there was war between Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> and Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> set the battle in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> with an army of valiant men of war, <char style="add">[even]</char> four hundred thousand chosen men: Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> also set the battle in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> against him with eight hundred thousand chosen men, <char style="add">[being]</char> mighty men of valour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> stood up upon mount Tz’marayim <char style="add">[Double Fleece of Wool]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and said, Hear me, you<char style="ord">i</char> Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Ought you<char style="ord">2f</char> not to know that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> gave the kingdom over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> forever, <char style="add">[even]</char> to him and to his sons by a covenant of salt?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Yet Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, the servant of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> the son of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, is risen up, and has rebelled against his lord.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And there are gathered unto him vain men, the children of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>, and have strengthened themselves against Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> the son of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, when Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> was young and tenderhearted, and could not withstand them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And now you<char style="ord">2f</char> think that is to withstand the kingdom of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in the hand of the sons of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> a great multitude, and <char style="add">[there are]</char> with you golden calves, which Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> made you for gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Have you<char style="ord">2f</char> not cast out the priests of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the sons of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and have made you priests after the manner of the nations of <char style="add">[other]</char> lands? so that whosoever comes to consecrate <char style="pn">(treat as set apart or separate unto God)</char> himself with a young bullock and seven rams, <char style="add">[the same]</char> may be a priest of <char style="add">[them that are]</char> no gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />But as for us, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and we have not forsaken him; and the priests, which minister unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[are]</char> the sons of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to] [wait]</char> upon <char style="add">[their]</char> business:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And they burn unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> every morning and every evening burnt sacrifices and sweet incense: the showbread also <char style="add">[set they in order]</char> upon the pure table; and the candlestick of gold with the lamps thereof, to burn every evening: for we keep the charge of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; but you<char style="ord">2f</char> have forsaken him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And, behold, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> himself <char style="add">[is]</char> with us for <char style="add">[our]</char> captain, and his priests with sounding trumpets to cry alarm against you. O people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, fight you<char style="ord">2f</char> not against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of your fathers; for you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not prosper.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />But Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> caused an ambush to come about behind them: so they were before Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and the ambush <char style="add">[was]</char> behind them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And when Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> looked back, behold, the battle <char style="add">[was]</char> before and behind: and they cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the priests sounded with the trumpets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> gave a shout: and as the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> shouted, it came to pass, that God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> struck Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> before Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> fled before Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: and God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> delivered them into their hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> and his people killed them with a great slaughter: so there fell down slain of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> five hundred thousand chosen men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Thus the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were brought under at that time, and the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> prevailed, because they relied upon the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> pursued after Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, and took cities from him, Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char> with the towns thereof, and Y’shanah <char style="add">[storage]</char> with the towns thereof, and ‘Efrayin <char style="add">[fawn-like]</char> with the towns thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Neither did Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> recover strength again in the days of Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char>: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> struck him, and he died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />But Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> waxed mighty, and married fourteen wives, and begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> twenty and two sons, and sixteen daughters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char>, and his ways, and his sayings, <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the story of the prophet ‘Iddo <char style="add">[His witness]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />So Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> his son reigned in his stead. In his days the land was quiet ten years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> good and right in the eyes of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />For he took away the altars of the strange <char style="add">[gods]</char>, and the high places, and broke down the images, and cut down the groves:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And commanded Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> to seek the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> f their fathers, and to do the law and the commandment.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Also he took away out of all the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> the high places and the images: and the kingdom was quiet before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he built fenced cities in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: for the land had rest, and he had no war in those years; because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had given him rest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Therefore he said unto Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, Let us build these cities, and make about <char style="add">[them]</char> walls, and towers, gates, and bars, <char style="add">[while]</char> the land <char style="add">[is]</char> yet before us; because we have sought the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, we have sought <char style="add">[him]</char>, and he has given us rest on every side. So they built and prospered.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> had an army <char style="add">[of men]</char> that bore targets and spears, out of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> three hundred thousand; and out of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, that bore shields and drew bows, two hundred and eighty thousand: all these <char style="add">[were]</char> mighty men of valour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And there came out against them Zerach <char style="add">[Rising]</char> the Cushi <char style="pn">(Ethiopian)</char> with an host of a thousand thousand, and three hundred chariots; and came unto Mareshah <char style="add">[Crest of a Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> went out against him, and they set the battle in array <char style="pn">(to put on; to clothe)</char> in the valley of Tz’fat <char style="add">[watch-tower]</char> at Mareshah <char style="add">[Crest of a Hill]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and said, LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[it is]</char> nothing with you<char style="ord">i</char> to help, whether with many, or with them that have no power: help us, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; for we rest on you<char style="ord">i</char>, and in you<char style="ord">i</char> name we go against this multitude. O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; let not man prevail against you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />So the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> struck the Cushi <char style="add">[Ethiopians]</char> before Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char>, and before Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>; and the Cushi <char style="add">[Ethiopians]</char> fled.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> and the people that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him pursued them unto Gera <char style="add">[A Grain]</char> r: and the Cushi <char style="add">[Ethiopians]</char> were overthrown, that they could not recover themselves; for they were destroyed before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and before his host; and they carried away very much spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they struck all the cities round about Gera <char style="add">[A Grain]</char> r; for the fear of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came upon them: and they spoiled all the cities; for there was exceeding much spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> in them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />They struck also the tents of cattle, and carried away sheep and camels in abundance, and returned to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the Spirit of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> came upon ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the son of ‘Oded <char style="add">[restorer]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he went out to meet Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char>, and said unto him, Hear you<char style="ord">2f</char> me, Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char>, and all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>; The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> with you, while you<char style="ord">2f</char> be with him; and if you<char style="ord">2f</char> seek him, he will be found of you; but if you<char style="ord">2f</char> forsake him, he will forsake you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now for a long season Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [has been]</char> without the true God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and without a teaching priest, and without law.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But when they in their trouble did turn unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and sought him, he was found of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And in those times <char style="add">[there was]</char> no peace to him that went out, nor to him that came in, but great vexations <char style="add">[were]</char> upon all the inhabitants of the countries.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And nation was destroyed of nation, and city of city: for God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> did vex them with all adversity.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Be you<char style="ord">2f</char> strong therefore, and let not your hands be weak: for your work shall be rewarded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And when Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> heard these words, and the prophecy of ‘Oded <char style="add">[restorer]</char> the prophet, he took courage, and put away the abominable idols out of all the land of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, and out of the cities which he had taken from mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and renewed the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that <char style="add">[was]</char> before the porch of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he gathered all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, and the strangers with them out of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> and M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, and out of Shim’on <char style="add">[he who hears]</char>: for they fell to him out of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in abundance, when they saw that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [was]</char> with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So they gathered themselves together at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> in the third month, in the fifteenth year of the reign of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And they offered unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> the same time, of the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> <char style="add">[which]</char> they had brought, seven hundred oxen and seven thousand sheep.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they entered into a covenant to seek the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers with all their heart and with all their soul;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />That whosoever would not seek the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> should be put to death, whether small or great, whether man or woman.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they swore unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with a loud voice, and with shouting, and with trumpets, and with cornets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> rejoiced at the oath: for they had sworn with all their heart, and sought him with their whole desire; and he was found of them: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> gave them rest round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And also <char style="add">[concerning]</char> Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression]</char> the mother of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> the king, he removed her from <char style="add">[being]</char> queen, because she had made an idol in a grove: and Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> cut down her idol, and stamped <char style="add">[it]</char>, and burnt <char style="add">[it]</char> at the brook Kidron <char style="add">[dark]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />But the high places were not taken away out of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: nevertheless the heart of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> was perfect all his days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he brought into the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> the things that his father had dedicated, and that he himself had dedicated, silver, and gold, and vessels.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And there was no <char style="add">[more]</char> war unto the five and thirtieth year of the reign of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />In the six and thirtieth year of the reign of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came up against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and built Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, to the intent that he might let none go out or come in to Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> brought out silver and gold out of the treasures of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> and of the king’s house, and sent to Ben <char style="add">[son]</char> -Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char> king of Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, that dwelt at Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[There is]</char> a league between me and you<char style="ord">i</char>, as <char style="add">[there was]</char> between my father and you<char style="ord">i</char> father: behold, I have sent you<char style="ord">i</char> silver and gold; go, break you<char style="ord">i</char> league with Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that he may depart from me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Ben <char style="add">[son]</char> -Hadad [son of the <char style="pn">(false god)</char> Hadad] listened unto king Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char>, and sent the captains of his armies against the cities of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and they struck ‘Iyon <char style="add">[a ruin]</char>, and Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, and Avel-Mayim <char style="add">[meadow of waters]</char>, and all the store cities of Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> heard <char style="add">[it]</char>, that he left off building of Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, and let his work cease.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> the king took all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>; and they carried away the stones of Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, and the timber thereof, which Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> was building; and he built with that Geva <char style="add">[hill]</char> and Mitzpah <char style="add">[watchtower]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And at that time Hanani <char style="add">[gracious]</char> the seer came to Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and said unto him, Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have relied on the king of Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, and not relied on the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, therefore is the host of the king of Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> escaped out of you<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Were not the Cushi <char style="add">[Ethiopians]</char> and the Luvim <char style="add">[empty-hearted]</char> a huge host, with very many chariots and horsemen? yet, because you<char style="ord">i</char> did rely on the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, he delivered them into your<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For the eyes of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> run to and fro throughout the whole earth, to show himself strong in the behalf of <char style="add">[them]</char> whose heart <char style="add">[is]</char> perfect toward him. Herein you<char style="ord">i</char> have done foolishly: therefore from from this time forth <char style="pn">(from now on)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall have wars.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> was exceedingly angry with the seer, and put him in a prison house; for <char style="add">[he was]</char> in a rage with him because of this <char style="add">[thing]</char>. And Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> oppressed <char style="add">[some]</char> of the people the same time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And, behold, the acts of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char>, first and last, lo, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the book of the kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> in the thirty and ninth year of his reign was diseased in his feet, until his disease <char style="add">[was]</char> exceeding <char style="add">[great]</char>: yet in his disease he sought not to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, but to the physicians.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> slept with his fathers, and died in the one and fortieth year of his reign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they buried him in his own sepulchres, which he had made for himself in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and laid him in the bed which was filled with sweet odours and diverse kinds <char style="add">[of spices]</char> prepared by the apothecaries’ are: and they made a very great burning for him.</para>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> his son reigned in his stead, and strengthened himself against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he placed forces in all the fenced cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and set garrisons in the land of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and in the cities of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, which Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> his father had taken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was with Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, because he walked in the first ways of his father David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and sought not unto Ba’alim <char style="add">[lords (false gods)]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But sought to the <char style="add">[LORD-Yehōvah (Messiah Pre-Incarnate)]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of his father, and walked in his commandments, and not after the doings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Therefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> established the kingdom in his hand; and all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> brought to Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> presents; and he had riches and honour in abundance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And his heart was lifted up in the ways of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: moreover he took away the high places and groves out of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Also in the third year of his reign he sent to his princes, <char style="add">[even]</char> to Ben-Chayil <char style="add">[son of strength]</char>, and to ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char>, and to Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, and to N’tan’el <char style="add">[God’s Gift]</char>, and to Mikhayah <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, to teach in the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And with them <char style="add">[he sent]</char> Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>, and N’tanyah <char style="add">[given of Yehovah]</char>, and Z’vadyah <char style="add">[endowment of Yehovah]</char>, and ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char>, and Sh’miramot <char style="add">[name of heights]</char>, and Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has given]</char>, and Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char>, and Toviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is good]</char>, and Tobadonijah, Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>; and with them Elishama <char style="add">[My God has Heard]</char> and Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char>, priests.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And they taught in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and <char style="add">[had]</char> the book of the law of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with them, and went about throughout all the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and taught the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the fear of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> fell upon all the kingdoms of the lands that <char style="add">[were]</char> round about Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, so that they made no war against Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Also <char style="add">[some]</char> of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> brought Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> presents, and tribute silver; and the Arabians brought him flocks, seven thousand and seven hundred rams, and seven thousand and seven hundred he goats.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> waxed great exceedingly; and he built in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> castles, and cities of store.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he had much business in the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: and the men of war, mighty men of valour, <char style="add">[were]</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[are]</char> the of them according to the house of their fathers: Of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, the captains of thousands; ‘Adnach <char style="add">[pleasure]</char> the chief, and with him mighty men of valour three hundred thousand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And next to him <char style="add">[was]</char> Y’hochanan <char style="add">[Yehovah has graced]</char> the captain, and with him two hundred and eighty thousand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And next him <char style="add">[was]</char> ‘Amasyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is strength]</char> the son of Zikhri <char style="add">[Illustrious]</char>, who willingly offered himself unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and with him two hundred thousand mighty men of valour.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>; El-yada <char style="add">[God knows]</char> a mighty man of valour, and with him armed men with bow and shield two hundred thousand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And next him <char style="add">[was]</char> Y’hozavad <char style="add">[Yehovah has endowed]</char>, and with him an hundred and eighty thousand ready prepared for the war.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />These waited on the king, beside <char style="add">[those]</char> whom the king put in the fenced cities throughout all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> had riches and honour in abundance, and joined affinity <char style="pn">(to become an in-law)</char> with Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And after <char style="add">[certain]</char> years he went down to Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>. And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> killed sheep and oxen for him in abundance, and for the people that <char style="add">[he had]</char> with him, and persuaded him to go up <char style="add">[with him]</char> to Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, Will you<char style="ord">i</char> go with me to Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>? And he answered him, I <char style="add">[am]</char> as you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char>, and my people as you<char style="ord">i</char> people; and <char style="add">[we will be]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char> in the war.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> said unto the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Enquire, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, at the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Therefore the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> gathered together of prophets four hundred men, and said unto them, Shall we go to Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char> to battle, or shall I refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char>? And they said, Go up; for God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> will deliver <char style="add">[it]</char> into the king’s hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> said, <char style="add">[Is there]</char> not here a prophet of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> besides, that we might enquire of him?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, <char style="add">[There is]</char> yet one man, by whom we may enquire of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: but I hate him; for he never prophesied good unto me, but always evil: the same <char style="add">[is]</char> Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> the son of Yimlah <char style="add">[whom God will fill up]</char>. And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> said, Let not the king say so.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> called for one <char style="add">[of his]</char> officers, and said, Fetch quickly Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> the son of Yimlah <char style="add">[whom God will fill up]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> sat either of them on his throne, clothed in <char style="add">[their]</char> robes, and they sat in a void place at the entering in of the gate of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>; and all the prophets prophesied before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char> the son of Kena’anah <char style="add">[trader]</char> had made him horns of iron, and said, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, With these you<char style="ord">i</char> shall push Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> until they be consumed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And all the prophets prophesied so, saying, Go up to Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>, and prosper: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall deliver <char style="add">[it]</char> into the hand of the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the messenger that went to call Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> spoke to him, saying, Behold, the words of the prophets <char style="add">[declare]</char> good to the king with one assent <char style="pn">(accord; agreement)</char>; let you<char style="ord">i</char> word therefore, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, be like one of theirs, and speak you<char style="ord">i</char> good.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, even what my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> says, that will I speak.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And when he was come to the king, the king said unto him, Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, shall we go to Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char> to battle, or shall I refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char>? And he said, Go you<char style="ord">2f</char> up, and prosper, and they shall be delivered into your hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the king said to him, How many times shall I adjure <char style="pn">(to command under oath or threat)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> that you<char style="ord">i</char> say nothing but the tto me in the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Then he said, I did see all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> scattered upon the mountains, as sheep that have no shepherd: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, These have no master; let them return <char style="add">[therefore]</char> every man to his house in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said to Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, Did I not tell you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[that]</char> he would not prophesy good unto me, but evil?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Again he said, Therefore hear the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; I saw the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sitting upon his throne, and all the army of heaven standing on his right hand and <char style="add">[on]</char> his left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, Who shall entice Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that he may go up and fall at Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>? And one spoke saying after this manner, and another saying after that manner.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then there came out a spirit, and stood before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, I will entice him. And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Wherewith?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And he said, I will go out, and be a lying spirit in the mouth of all his prophets. And <char style="add">[the LORD-Yehōvah (Messiah Pre-Incarnate)]</char> said, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall entice <char style="add">[him]</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall also prevail: go out, and do <char style="add">[even]</char> so.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Now therefore, behold, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has put a lying spirit in the mouth of these you<char style="ord">i</char> prophets, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has spoken evil against you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Then Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char> the son of Kena’anah <char style="add">[trader]</char> came near, and struck Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> upon the cheek, and said, Which way went the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> from me to speak unto you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> said, Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall see on that day when you<char style="ord">i</char> shall go into an inner chamber to hide yourself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Then the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said, Take you<char style="ord">2f</char> Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, and carry him back to ‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman]</char> the governor of the city, and to Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> the king’s son;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And say, Thus says the king, Put <char style="add">[a bow]</char> this <char style="add">[fellow]</char> in the prison, and feed him with bread of affliction and with water of affliction, until I return in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> said, If you<char style="ord">i</char> certainly return in peace, <char style="add">[then]</char> has not the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoken by me. And he said, Listen, all you<char style="ord">2f</char> people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />So the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> went up to Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, I will disguise myself, and will go to the battle; but put you<char style="ord">i</char> on you<char style="ord">i</char> robes. So the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> disguised himself; and they went to the battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Now the king of Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> had commanded the captains of the chariots that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him, saying, Fight you<char style="ord">2f</char> not with small or great, save only with the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the captains of the chariots saw Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, that they said, It <char style="add">[is]</char> the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>. Therefore they compassed about him to fight: but Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> cried out, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> helped him; and God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> moved them <char style="add">[to depart]</char> from him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />For it came to pass, that, when the captains of the chariots perceived that it was not the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, they turned back again from pursuing him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And a <char style="add">[certain]</char> man drew a bow at a venture, and struck the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> between the joints of the harness: therefore he said to his chariot man, Turn you<char style="ord">i</char> hand, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may carry me out of the host; for I am wounded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And the battle increased that day: howbeit the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> <char style="add">[himself]</char> up in <char style="add">[his]</char> chariot against the Aram <char style="add">[exalted] [Syrians]</char> until the even: and about the time of the sun going down he died.</para>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> returned to his house in peace to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> the son of Hanani <char style="add">[gracious]</char> the seer went out to meet him, and said to king Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, Should you<char style="ord">i</char> help the ungodly, and love them that hate the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>? therefore <char style="add">[is]</char> wrath upon you<char style="ord">i</char> from before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Nevertheless there are good things found in you<char style="ord">i</char>, in that you<char style="ord">i</char> have taken away the Asherot out of the land, and have prepared your<char style="ord">i</char> heart to seek God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> dwelt at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: and he went out again through the people from Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char> to mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and brought them back unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he set in the land throughout all the fenced cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, city by city,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And said to the judges, Take heed what you<char style="ord">2f</char> do: for you<char style="ord">2f</char> judge not for man, but for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, who <char style="add">[is]</char> with you in the judgment.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For what reason now let the fear of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> be upon you; take heed and do <char style="add">[it]</char>: for <char style="add">[there is]</char> no iniquity with the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, nor respect of persons, nor taking of gifts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Moreover in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> did Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> set of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and <char style="add">[of]</char> the priests, and of the chief of the fathers of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, for the judgment of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and for controversies, when they returned to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he charged them, saying, Thus shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> do in the fear of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, faithfully, and with a perfect heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And what cause whosoever shall come to you of your brethren that dwell in their cities, between blood and blood, between law and commandment, statutes and judgments, you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall even warn them that they trespass not against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and <char style="add">[so]</char> wrath come upon you, and upon your brethren: this do, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not trespass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And, behold, Amaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah speaks]</char> the chief priest <char style="add">[is]</char> over you in all matters of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and Z’vadyah <char style="add">[endowment of Yehovah]</char> the son of Yishma’el <char style="add">[God will hear]</char>, the ruler of the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, for all the king’s matters: also the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to] [shall be]</char> officers before you. Deal courageously, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall be with the good.</para>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />It came to pass after this also, <char style="add">[that]</char> the children of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and with them <char style="add">[other]</char> beside the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, came against Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> to battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then there came some that told Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, saying, There comes a great multitude against you<char style="ord">i</char> from beyond the sea on this side Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>; and, behold, they <char style="add">[be]</char> in Hatzatzon-Tamar <char style="add">[dividing the date-palm]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> ‘Ein-Gedi <char style="add">[Fount of the Kid]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> feared, and set himself to seek the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and proclaimed a fast throughout all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> gathered themselves together, to ask <char style="add">[help]</char> of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: even out of all the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> they came to seek the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> stood in the congregation of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, before the new court,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And said, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of our fathers, <char style="add">[are]</char> not you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in heaven? and rule <char style="add">[not]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> over all the kingdoms of the heathen? and in your<char style="ord">i</char> hand <char style="add">[is there not]</char> power and might, so that none is able that is to withstand you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Are]</char> not you<char style="ord">i</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, <char style="add">[who]</char> did drive out the inhabitants of this land before your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and gave it to the seed of Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> friend forever?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And they dwelt in it, and have built you<char style="ord">i</char> a sanctuary in it for your<char style="ord">i</char> name, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />If, <char style="add">[when]</char> evil comes upon us, <char style="add">[as]</char> the sword, judgment, or pestilence, or famine, we stand before this house, and in your<char style="ord">i</char> presence, (for your<char style="ord">i</char> name <char style="add">[is]</char> in this house,) and cry unto you<char style="ord">i</char> in our affliction, then you<char style="ord">i</char> will hear and help.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And now, behold, the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> and Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> and mount Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char>, whom you<char style="ord">i</char> would not let Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> invade, when they came out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, but they turned from them, and destroyed them not;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Behold, <char style="add">[I say, how]</char> they reward us, to come to cast us out of your<char style="ord">i</char> possession, which you<char style="ord">i</char> have given us to inherit.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />O our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, will you<char style="ord">i</char> not judge them? for we have no might against this great company that comes against us; neither know we what to do: but our eyes <char style="add">[are]</char> upon you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> stood before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, with their little ones, their wives, and their children.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then upon Yachazi’el <char style="add">[beheld of God]</char> the son of Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, the son of B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char>, the son of Ye’i’el <char style="add">[God sweeps away]</char>, the son of Matanyah <char style="add">[gift of Yehovah]</char>, a Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> of the sons of Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char>, came the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in the midst of the congregation;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he said, Listen you<char style="ord">2f</char>, all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> king Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto you, Be not afraid nor dismayed by reason of this great multitude; for the battle <char style="add">[is]</char> not yours, but God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>’s.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Tomorrow go you<char style="ord">2f</char> down against them: behold, they come up by the cliff of Tzitz <char style="add">[flower]</char>; and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall find them at the end of the brook, before the wilderness of Yeru’el <char style="add">[taught by God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not <char style="add">[need]</char> to fight in this <char style="add">[battle]</char>: set yourselves, stand you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[still]</char>, and see the salvation of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with you, O Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: fear not, nor be dismayed; tomorrow go out against them: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[will be]</char> with you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> bowed his head with <char style="add">[his]</char> face to the ground: and all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> fell before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, worshipping the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, of the children of the K’hati, and of the children of the Korchi <char style="add">[of baldness]</char>, stood up to praise the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with a loud voice on high.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And they rose early in the morning, and went forth into the wilderness of T’koa <char style="add">[a stockade]</char>: and as they went forth, Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> stood and said, Hear me, O Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; Believe in the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, so shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> be established; believe his prophets, so shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> prosper.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And when he had consulted with the people, he appointed singers unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and that should praise the beauty of holiness, as they went out before the army, and to say, Praise the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; for his mercy <char style="add">[endures]</char> forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And when they began to sing and to praise, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> set ambushes against the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, and mount Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char>, which were come against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>; and they were smitten.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />For the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> and Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char> stood up against the inhabitants of mount Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char>, utterly to slay and destroy <char style="add">[them]</char>: and when they had made an end of the inhabitants of Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char>, every one helped to destroy another.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And when Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> came toward the watch tower in the wilderness, they looked unto the multitude, and, behold, they <char style="add">[were]</char> dead bodies fallen to the earth, and none escaped.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And when Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> and his people came to take away the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> of them, they found among them in abundance both riches with the dead bodies, and precious jewels, which they stripped off for themselves, more than they could carry away: and they were three days in gathering of the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>, it was so much.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And on the fourth day they assembled themselves in the valley of B’rakhah <char style="add">[blessing]</char>; for there they Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: therefore the name of the same place was called, The valley of B’rakhah <char style="add">[blessing]</char>, unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Then they returned, every man of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> in the forefront of them, to go again to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> with joy; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had made them to rejoice over their enemies.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And they came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> with psalteries and harps and trumpets unto the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And the fear of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was on all the kingdoms of <char style="add">[those]</char> countries, when they had heard that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> fought against the enemies of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />So the realm of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> was quiet: for his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> gave him rest round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> reigned over Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: <char style="add">[he was]</char> thirty and five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned twenty and five years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> ‘Azuvah <char style="add">[forsaken]</char> the daughter of Shilchi <char style="add">[armed]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And he walked in the way of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> his father, and departed not from it, doing <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />However the high places were not taken away: for as yet the people had not prepared their hearts unto the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, first and last, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the book of Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> the son of Hanani <char style="add">[gracious]</char>, who <char style="add">[is]</char> mentioned in the book of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And after this did Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> join himself with Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, who did very wickedly:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And he joined himself with him to make ships to go to Tarshish <char style="add">[yellow jasper]</char>: and they made the ships in ‘Etzyon-Gever <char style="add">[backbone of a man]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Then Eli’ezer <char style="add">[God is help]</char> the son of Dodavahu <char style="add">[beloved of Yehovah]</char> of Mareshah <char style="add">[Crest of a Hill]</char> prophesied against Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, saying, Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have joined yourself with Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has broken your<char style="ord">i</char> works. And the ships were broken, that they were not able to go to Tarshish <char style="add">[yellow jasper]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>. And Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he had brethren the sons of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char>, and Jehiel, and Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, and ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char>, and Mikha’el <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>, and Sh’fatyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>: all these <char style="add">[were]</char> the sons of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And their father gave them great gifts of silver, and of gold, and of precious things, with fenced cities in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: but the kingdom gave he to Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char>; because he <char style="add">[was]</char> the firstborn.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Now when Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> was risen up to the kingdom of his father, he strengthened himself, and killed all his brethren with the sword, and <char style="add">[diverse]</char> also of the princes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted] [was]</char> thirty and two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eight years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he walked in the way of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, like as did the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>: for he had the daughter of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> to wife: and he wrought <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the eyes of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />However the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> would not destroy the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, because of the covenant that he had made with David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and as he promised to give a light to him and to his sons forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />In his days the Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char> revolted from under the dominion of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and made themselves a king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> went forth with his princes, and all his chariots with him: and he rose up by night, and struck the Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char> which compassed him in, and the captains of the chariots.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So the Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char> revolted from under the hand of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> unto this day. The same time <char style="add">[also]</char> did Livnah <char style="add">[Pavement]</char> revolt from under his hand; because he had forsaken the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of his fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Moreover he made high places in the mountains of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and caused the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to commit fornication, and compelled Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised] [thereto]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And there came a writing to him from Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> the prophet, saying, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> father, Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have not walked in the ways of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> father, nor in the ways of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />But have walked in the way of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and have made Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to go a whoring, like to the cult prostitution of the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, and also have slain you<char style="ord">i</char> brethren of you<char style="ord">i</char> father’s house, <char style="add">[which were]</char> better than yourself:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Behold, with a great plague will the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> strike you<char style="ord">i</char> people, and you<char style="ord">i</char> children, and you<char style="ord">i</char> wives, and all you<char style="ord">i</char> goods:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[shall have]</char> great sickness by disease of you<char style="ord">i</char> bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char>, until you<char style="ord">i</char> bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char> fall out by reason of the sickness day by day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Moreover the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> stirred up against Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> the spirit of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and of the Arabians, that <char style="add">[were]</char> near the Cushi <char style="add">[Ethiopians]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And they came up into Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and broke into it, and carried away all the substance that was found in the king’s house, and his sons also, and his wives; so that there was never a son left him, save Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char>, the youngest of his sons.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And after all this the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> struck him in his bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char> with an incurable disease.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And it came to pass, that in process of time, after the end of two years, his bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char> fell out by reason of his sickness: so he died of sore diseases. And his people made no burning for him, like the burning of his fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Thirty and two years old was he when he began to reign, and he reigned in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> eight years, and departed without being desired. However they buried him in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, but not in the sepulchres of the kings.</para>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> made Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> his youngest son king in his stead: for the band of men that came with the Arabians to the camp had slain all the eldest. So Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> the son of Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> reigned.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Forty and two years old <char style="add">[was]</char> Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> when he began to reign, and he reigned one year in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. His mother’s name also <char style="add">[was]</char> ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char> the daughter of ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />He also walked in the ways of the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>: for his mother was his counsellor to do wickedly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />For what reason he did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> like the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>: for they were his counsellors after the death of his father to his destruction.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />He walked also after their counsel, and went with Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> the son of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to war against Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> king of Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> at Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>: and the Aram <char style="add">[exalted] [Syrians]</char> struck Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he returned to be healed in Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char> because of the wounds which were given him at Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, when he fought with Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> king of Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>. And ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the son of Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> went down to see Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> the son of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> at Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, because he was sick.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the destruction of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> was of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> by coming to Yoram <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char>: for when he was come, he went out with Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> against Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> the son of Nimshi <char style="add">[rescued]</char>, whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had anointed to cut off the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And it came to pass, that, when Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> was executing judgment upon the house of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, and found the princes of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and the sons of the brethren of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>, that ministered to Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>, he killed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he sought Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>: and they caught him, (for he was hid in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>,) and brought him to Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char>: and when they had slain him, they buried him: Because, said they, he <char style="add">[is]</char> the son of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, who sought the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with all his heart. So the house of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> had no power to keep still the kingdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />But when ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char> the mother of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> saw that her son was dead, she arose and destroyed all the seed royal of the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />But Y’hoshav’at <char style="add">[Yehovah is an oath]</char>, the daughter of the king, took Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> the son of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>, and stole him from among the king’s sons that were slain, and put him and his nurse in a bedchamber. So Y’hoshav’at <char style="add">[Yehovah is an oath]</char>, the daughter of king Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char>, the wife of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest, (for she was the sister of Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char>,) hid him from ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char>, so that she killed him not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he was with them hid in the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> six years: and ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char> reigned over the land.</para>
  <chapter number="23" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And in the seventh year Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> strengthened himself, and took the captains of hundreds, ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the son of Yerocham <char style="add">[showing pity]</char>, and Yishma’el <char style="add">[God will hear]</char> the son of Y’hochanan <char style="add">[Yehovah has graced]</char>, and ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the son of ‘Oved <char style="add">[serving]</char>, and Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char> the son of ‘Adayah <char style="add">[Yehovah has adorned Himself]</char>, and Elishafat <char style="add">[my God has judged]</char> the son of Zikhri <char style="add">[Illustrious]</char>, into covenant with him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And they went about in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and gathered the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> out of all the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and the chief of the fathers of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and they came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And all the congregation made a covenant with the king in the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. And he said unto them, Behold, the king’s son shall reign, as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has said of the sons of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />This <char style="add">[is]</char> the thing that you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall do; A third part of you entering on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, of the priests and of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, <char style="add">[shall be]</char> porters of the doors;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And a third part <char style="add">[shall be]</char> at the king’s house; and a third part at the gate of the foundation: and all the people <char style="add">[shall be]</char> in the courts of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />But let none come into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, save the priests, and they that minister of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>; they shall go in, for they <char style="add">[are]</char> holy: but all the people shall keep the watch of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> shall compass <char style="pn">(go around, encircle; encompass)</char> the king round about, every man with his weapons in his hand; and whosoever <char style="add">[else]</char> comes into the house, he shall be put to death: but be you<char style="ord">2f</char> with the king when he comes in, and when he goes out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />So the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> and all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> did according to all things that Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest had commanded, and took every man his men that were to come in on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, with them that were to go <char style="add">[out]</char> on the Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>: for Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest dismissed not the courses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Moreover Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest delivered to the captains of hundreds spears, and bucklers, and shields, that <char style="add">[had been]</char> king David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s, which <char style="add">[were]</char> in the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he set all the people, every man having his weapon in his hand, from the right side of the temple to the left side of the temple, along by the altar and the temple, by the king round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then they brought out the king’s son, and put upon him the crown, and <char style="add">[gave him]</char> the testimony, and made him king. And Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> and his sons anointed him, and said, Long live the king!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Now when ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char> heard the noise of the people running and praising the king, she came to the people into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And she looked, and, behold, the king stood at his pillar at the entering in, and the princes and the trumpets by the king: and all the people of the land rejoiced, and sounded with trumpets, also the singers with instruments of music, and such as taught to sing praise. Then ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char> rent her clothes, and said, Treason, Treason.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest brought out the captains of hundreds that were set over the host, and said unto them, Have her forth of the ranges: and whoso follows her, let him be slain with the sword. For the priest said, Slay her not in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />So they laid hands on her; and when she was come to the entering of the horse gate by the king’s house, they killed her there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> made a covenant between him, and between all the people, and between the king, that they should be the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then all the people went to the house of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and broke it down, and broke his altars and his images in pieces, and killed Mattan <char style="add">[a gift]</char> the priest of Ba’al [lord (a false god)] before the altars.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Also Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> appointed the offices of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> by the hand of the priests the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, whom David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> had distributed in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to offer the burnt offerings of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as <char style="add">[it is]</char> written in the law of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, with rejoicing and with singing, <char style="add">[as it was ordained]</char> by David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he set the porters at the gates of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that none <char style="add">[which was]</char> unclean in any thing should enter in.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he took the captains of hundreds, and the nobles, and the governors of the people, and all the people of the land, and brought down the king from the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and they came through the high gate into the king’s house, and set the king upon the throne of the kingdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And all the people of the land rejoiced: and the city was quiet, after that they had slain ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char> with the sword.</para>
  <chapter number="24" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord] [was]</char> seven years old when he began to reign, and he reigned forty years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. His mother’s name also <char style="add">[was]</char> Tzivyah <char style="add">[roe]</char> of Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> all the days of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> took for him two wives; and he begat <char style="pn">(to be father of; be ancestor of)</char> sons and daughters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it came to pass after this, <char style="add">[that]</char> Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> was minded to repair the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he gathered together the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and said to them, Go out unto the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and gather of all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> money to repair the house of your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> from year to year, and see that you<char style="ord">2f</char> hasten the matter. However the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> hastened <char style="add">[it]</char> not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the king called for Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the chief, and said unto him, Why have you<char style="ord">i</char> not required of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> to bring in out of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and out of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> the collection, <char style="add">[according to the commandment]</char> of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> the servant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and of the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, for the tabernacle of witness?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For the sons of ‘Atalyahu <char style="add">[afflicted of the Lord]</char>, that wicked woman, had broken up the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; and also all the dedicated things of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> did they bestow upon Ba’alim <char style="add">[lords (false gods)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And at the king’s commandment they made a chest, and set it without at the gate of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And they made a proclamation through Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, to bring in to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> the collection <char style="add">[that]</char> Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> the servant of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [laid]</char> upon Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And all the princes and all the people rejoiced, and brought in, and cast into the chest, until they had made an end.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Now it came to pass, that at what time the chest was brought unto the king’s office by the hand of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and when they saw that <char style="add">[there was]</char> much money, the king’s scribe and the high priest’s officer came and emptied the chest, and took it, and carried it to his place again. Thus they did day by day, and gathered money in abundance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the king and Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> gave it to such as did the work of the service of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and hired masons and carpenters to repair the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and also such as wrought iron and brass to mend the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />So the workmen wrought, and the work was perfected by them, and they set the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in his state, and strengthened it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And when they had finished <char style="add">[it]</char>, they brought the rest of the money before the king and Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>, whereof were made vessels for the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> vessels to minister, and to offer <char style="add">[withal]</char>, and spoons, and vessels of gold and silver. And they offered burnt offerings in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> continually all the days of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />But Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> waxed old, and was full of days when he died; an hundred and thirty years old <char style="add">[was he]</char> when he died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And they buried him in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> among the kings, because he had done good in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, both toward God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and toward his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Now after the death of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> came the princes of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and made obesiance <char style="pn">(bowing or kneeling in respect)</char> to the king. Then the king listened unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And they left the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers, and served groves and idols: and wrath came upon Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> for this their trespass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Yet he sent prophets to them, to bring them again unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and they testified against them: but they would not give ear.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the Spirit of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> came upon Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest, which stood above the people, and said unto them, Thus says God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, Why transgress you<char style="ord">2f</char> the commandments of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> cannot prosper? because you<char style="ord">2f</char> have forsaken the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, he has also forsaken you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And they conspired against him, and stoned him with stones at the commandment of the king in the court of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Thus Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> the king remembered not the kindness which Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> his father had done to him, but killed his son. And when he died, he said, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> look upon <char style="add">[it]</char>, and require <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And it came to pass at the end of the year, <char style="add">[that]</char> the host of Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> came up against him: and they came to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and destroyed all the princes of the people from among the people, and sent all the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> of them unto the king of Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />For the army of the Aram <char style="add">[exalted] [Syrians]</char> came with a small company of men, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> delivered a very great host into their hand, because they had forsaken the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers. So they executed judgment against Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And when they were departed from him, <char style="pn">(for they left him in great diseases,)</char> his own servants conspired against him for the blood of the sons of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> the priest, and killed him on his bed, and he died: and they buried him in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, but they buried him not in the sepulchres of the kings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And these are they that conspired against him; Zavad <char style="add">[he endows]</char> the son of Shim’at <char style="add">[report]</char> an ‘Amonit <char style="add">[tribal]</char>, and Y’hozavad <char style="add">[Yehovah has endowed]</char> the son of Shimrith a Moaviah [from father: what father?].</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Now <char style="add">[concerning]</char> his sons, and the greatness of the burdens <char style="add">[laid]</char> upon him, and the repairing of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the story of the book of the kings. And Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="25" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty] [was]</char> twenty and five years old <char style="add">[when]</char> he began to reign, and he reigned twenty and nine years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Y’ho’adan <char style="add">[Yehovah delights]</char> of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, but not with a perfect heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Now it came to pass, when the kingdom was established to him, that he killed his servants that had killed the king his father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But he killed not their children, but <char style="add">[did]</char> as <char style="add">[it is]</char> written in the law in the book of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, where the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded, saying, The fathers shall not die for the children, neither shall the children die for the fathers, but every man shall die for his own sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Moreover Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> gathered Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> together, and made them captains over thousands, and captains over hundreds, according to the houses of <char style="add">[their]</char> fathers, throughout all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>: and he numbered them from twenty years old and above, and found them three hundred thousand choice <char style="add">[men, able]</char> to go forth to war, that could handle spear and shield.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />He hired also an hundred thousand mighty men of valour out of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> for an hundred talents of silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />But there came a man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> to him, saying, O king, let not the army of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> go with you<char style="ord">i</char>; for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> not with Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[that is to say, with]</char> all the children of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But if you<char style="ord">i</char> will go, do <char style="add">[it]</char>, be strong for the battle: God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> shall make you<char style="ord">i</char> fall before the enemy: for God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The any Powered]</char> has power to help, and to cast down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> said to the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, But what shall we do for the hundred talents which I have given to the army of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? And the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> answered, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> is able to give you<char style="ord">i</char> much more than this.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Then Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> separated them, <char style="add">[that is to say]</char>, the army that was come to him out of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, to go home again: wherefore their anger was greatly kindled against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and they returned home in great anger.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> strengthened himself, and led forth his people, and went to the valley of salt, and struck of the children of Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char> ten thousand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And <char style="add">[other]</char> ten thousand <char style="add">[left]</char> alive did the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> carry away captive, and brought them unto the top of the rock, and cast them down from the top of the rock, that they all were broken in pieces.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />But the soldiers of the army which Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> sent back, that they should not go with him to battle, fell upon the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, from Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> even unto Beit-Horon <char style="add">[House of Hollowness]</char>, and struck three thousand of them, and took much spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Now it came to pass, after that Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> was come from the slaughter of the Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char>, that he brought the gods of the children of Se’ir <char style="add">[Shaggy]</char>, and set them up <char style="add">[to be]</char> his gods, and bowed down himself before them, and burned incense unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />For what reason the anger of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was kindled against Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char>, and he sent unto him a prophet, which said unto him, Why have you<char style="ord">i</char> sought after the gods of the people, which could not deliver their own people out of you<char style="ord">i</char> hand?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it came to pass, as he talked with him, that <char style="add">[the king]</char> said unto him, Are you<char style="ord">i</char> made of the king’s counsel? refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char>; why should you<char style="ord">i</char> be smitten? Then the prophet forbare, and said, I know that God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> has determined to destroy you<char style="ord">i</char>, because you<char style="ord">i</char> have done this, and have not listened unto my counsel.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Then Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> took advice, and sent to Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char>, the son of Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char>, the son of Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char>, king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, Come, let us see one another in the face.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sent to Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, saying, The thistle that <char style="add">[was]</char> in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char> sent to the cedar that <char style="add">[was]</char> in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, saying, Give you<char style="ord">i</char> daughter to my son to wife: and there passed by a wild beast that <char style="add">[was]</char> in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, and trampled down the thistle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> say, Lo, you<char style="ord">i</char> have smitten the Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char>; and you<char style="ord">i</char> heart lifts you<char style="ord">i</char> up to boast: abide now at home; why should you<char style="ord">i</char> meddle to <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> hurt, that you<char style="ord">i</char> should fall, <char style="add">[even]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char>, and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />But Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> would not hear; for it <char style="add">[came]</char> of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that he might deliver them into the hand <char style="add">[of their enemies]</char>, because they sought after the gods of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />So Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went up; and they saw one another in the face, <char style="add">[both]</char> he and Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, at Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char>, which <char style="add">[belongs]</char> to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> was put to the worse before Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and they fled every man to his tent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> took Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char>, the son of Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char>, at Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char>, and brought him to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and broke down the wall of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> from the gate of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> to the corner gate, four hundred cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And <char style="add">[he took]</char> all the gold and the silver, and all the vessels that were found in the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> with ‘Oved-Edom <char style="add">[servant of Edom]</char>, and the treasures of the king’s house, the hostages also, and returned to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> the son of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> lived after the death of Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> son of Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> fifteen years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char>, first and last, behold, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Now after the time that Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> did turn away from following the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> they made a conspiracy against him in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>; and he fled to Lakhish <char style="add">[Invincible]</char>: but they sent to Lakhish <char style="add">[Invincible]</char> after him, and killed him there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And they brought him upon horses, and buried him with his fathers in the city of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="26" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then all the people of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> took ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char>, who <char style="add">[was]</char> sixteen years old, and made him king in the room of his father Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />He built Elot <char style="add">[grove of lofty trees]</char>, and restored it to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, after that the king slept with his fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Sixteen years old <char style="add">[was]</char> ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty and two years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. His mother’s name also <char style="add">[was]</char> Y’kholyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is able]</char> of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, according to all that his father Amatzyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char> did.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he sought God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in the days of Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, who had understanding in the visions of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: and as long as he sought the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> made him to prosper.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he went forth and warred against the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and broke down the wall of Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, and the wall of Yavneh <char style="add">[building of God]</char>, and the wall of Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char>, and built cities about Ashdod <char style="add">[powerful]</char>, and among the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> helped him against the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and against the Arabians that dwelt in Gur-Ba’al <char style="add">[dwelling of lord]</char>, and the Me’unim <char style="add">[habitations]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> gave gifts to ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char>: and his name spread abroad <char style="add">[even]</char> to the entering in of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>; for he strengthened <char style="add">[himself]</char> exceedingly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Moreover ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> built towers in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> at the corner gate, and at the valley gate, and at the turning <char style="add">[of the wall]</char>, and fortified them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Also he built towers in the desert, and excavated many wells: for he had much cattle, both in the low country, and in the plains: husbandmen <char style="add">[also]</char>, and vine dressers in the mountains, and in Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>: for he loved husbandry.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Moreover ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> had an host of fighting men, that went out to war by bands, according to the number of their account by the hand of Ye’i’el <char style="add">[God sweeps away]</char> the scribe and Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char> the ruler, under the hand of Hananyah <char style="add">[God has favoured]</char>, <char style="add">[one]</char> of the king’s captains.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />The whole number of the chief of the fathers of the mighty men of valour <char style="add">[were]</char> two thousand and six hundred.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And under their hand <char style="add">[was]</char> an army, three hundred thousand and seven thousand and five hundred, that made war with mighty power, to help the king against the enemy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> prepared for them throughout all the host shields, and spears, and helmets, and habergeons, and bows, and slings <char style="add">[to cast]</char> stones.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he made in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> engines, invented by cunning men, to be on the towers and upon the bulwarks, to shoot arrows and great stones withal. And his name spread far abroad; for he was marvellously helped, till he was strong.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />But when he was strong, his heart was lifted up to <char style="add">[his]</char> destruction: for he transgressed against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and went into the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to burn incense upon the altar of incense.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the priest went in after him, and with him eighty priests of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[that were]</char> valiant men:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And they withstood ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> the king, and said unto him, <char style="add">[It pertains]</char> not unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char>, to burn incense unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, but to the priests the sons of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>, that are consecrated to burn incense: go out of the sanctuary; for you<char style="ord">i</char> have trespassed; neither <char style="add">[shall it be]</char> for you<char style="ord">i</char> honour from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Then ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> was exceedingly angry, and <char style="add">[had]</char> a censer in his hand to burn incense: and while he was exceedingly angry with the priests, the leprosy even rose up in his forehead before the priests in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, from beside the incense altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the chief priest, and all the priests, looked upon him, and, behold, he <char style="add">[was]</char> leprous in his forehead, and they thrust him out from there; yes, himself hasted also to go out, because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had smitten him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> the king was a leper unto the day of his death, and dwelt in a several house, <char style="add">[being]</char> a leper; for he was cut off from the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> his son <char style="add">[was]</char> over the king’s house, judging the people of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char>, first and last, did Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> the prophet, the son of Amotz <char style="add">[strong]</char>, write.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />So ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> slept with his fathers, and they buried him with his fathers in the field of the burial which <char style="add">[belonged]</char> to the kings; for they said, He <char style="add">[is]</char> a leper: and Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="27" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect] [was]</char> twenty and five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. His mother’s name also <char style="add">[was]</char> Yerushah <char style="add">[dispossessor]</char>, the daughter of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, according to all that his father ‘Uziyah <char style="add">[my strength is Yehovah]</char> did: howbeit he entered not into the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And the people did yet corruptly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />He built the high gate of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and on the wall of ‘Ofel <char style="add">[hill]</char> he built much.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Moreover he built cities in the mountains of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and in the forests he built castles and towers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />He fought also with the king of the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and prevailed against them. And the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> gave him the same year an hundred talents of silver, and ten thousand measures of wheat, and ten thousand of barley. So much did the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char> pay unto him, both the second year, and the third.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> became mighty, because he prepared his ways before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char>, and all his wars, and his ways, lo, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the book of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />He was five and twenty years old when he began to reign, and reigned sixteen years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Toram <char style="add">[Yehovah is Perfect]</char> slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="28" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped] [was]</char> twenty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: but he did not <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, like David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For he walked in the ways of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and made also molten images for Ba’alim <char style="add">[lords (false gods)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Moreover he burnt incense in the valley of the son of Hinnom <char style="add">[Lamentation]</char>, and burnt his children in the fire, after the abominations of the heathen whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had cast out before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />He sacrificed also and burnt incense in the high places, and on the hills, and under every green tree.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />For what reason the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> delivered him into the hand of the king of Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>; and they struck him, and carried away a great multitude of them captives, and brought <char style="add">[them]</char> to Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>. And he was also delivered into the hand of the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, who struck him with a great slaughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For Pekach <char style="add">[opened]</char> the son of Remalyahu <char style="add">[protected by Yehovah]</char> killed in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> an hundred and twenty thousand in one day, <char style="add">[which were]</char> all valiant men; because they had forsaken the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Zikhri <char style="add">[Illustrious]</char>, a mighty man of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, killed Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char> the king’s son, and ‘Azrikam <char style="add">[help against the enemy]</char> the governor of the house, and Elkanah <char style="add">[God Has Taken Possession] [that was]</char> next to the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> carried away captive of their brethren two hundred thousand, women, sons, and daughters, and took also away much spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> from them, and brought the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But a prophet of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was there, whose name <char style="add">[was]</char> ‘Oded <char style="add">[restorer]</char>: and he went out before the host that came to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and said unto them, Behold, because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of your fathers was exceedingly angry with Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, he has delivered them into your hand, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> have slain them in a rage <char style="add">[that]</char> reaches up unto heaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And now you<char style="ord">2f</char> purpose to keep under the children of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> for bondmen and bondwomen unto you: <char style="add">[but are there]</char> not with you, even with you, sins against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Now hear me therefore, and deliver the captives again, which you<char style="ord">2f</char> have taken captive of your brethren: for the fierce wrath of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> upon you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then certain of the heads of the children of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the son of Yochanan <char style="add">[Yehovah has graced]</char>, Berekhyah <char style="add">[Yehovah blesses]</char> the son of Meshillemot <char style="add">[recompense]</char>, and Y’chizkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has made me strong]</char> the son of Shalum <char style="add">[retribution]</char>, and ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char> the son of Hadlai <char style="add">[rest of God]</char>, stood up against them that came from the war,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And said unto them, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not bring in the captives here: for whereas we have offended against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[already]</char>, you<char style="ord">2f</char> intend to add <char style="add">[more]</char> to our sins and to our trespass: for our trespass is great, and <char style="add">[there is]</char> fierce wrath against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />So the armed men left the captives and the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> before the princes and all the congregation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the men which were expressed by name rose up, and took the captives, and with the spoil <char style="pn">(plunder; prey; booty)</char> clothed all that were naked among them, and arrayed them, and shod them, and gave them to eat and to drink, and anointed them, and carried all the feeble of them upon asses, and brought them to Yericho <char style="add">[Its Moon]</char>, the city of palm trees, to their brethren: then they returned to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />At that time did king Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> send unto the kings of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem [name] (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> to help him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />For again the Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char> had come and smitten Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and carried away captives.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />The P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char> also had invaded the cities of the low country, and of the south of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and had taken Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char>, and Ayalon <char style="add">[Field of Deer]</char>, and G’derot <char style="add">[Walls]</char>, and Sokho <char style="add">[bushy]</char> with the villages thereof, and Timnah <char style="add">[Portion]</char> with the villages thereof, Gimzo <char style="add">[fertile sycamores]</char> also and the villages thereof: and they dwelt there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />For the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> brought Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> low because of Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; for he made Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> naked, and transgressed sore against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Tigat-Piln’eser <char style="add">[you will uncover the wonderful bond]</char> king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> (the land of the sons of Shem <char style="add">[name]</char> <char style="pn">(name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> came unto him, and distressed him, but strengthened him not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />For Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> took away a portion <char style="add">[out]</char> of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and <char style="add">[out]</char> of the house of the king, and of the princes, and gave <char style="add">[it]</char> unto the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem [name] (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>: but he helped him not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And in the time of his distress did he trespass yet more against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: this <char style="add">[is that]</char> king Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />For he sacrificed unto the gods of Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, which struck him: and he said, Because the gods of the kings of Aram <char style="add">[exalted]</char> <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> help them, <char style="add">[therefore]</char> will I sacrifice to them, that they may help me. But they were the ruin of him, and of all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> gathered together the vessels of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and cut in pieces the vessels of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and shut up the doors of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and he made him altars in every corner of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And in every single <char style="pn">(each one separately)</char> city of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> he made high places to burn incense unto other gods, and provoked to anger the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of his fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Now the rest of his acts and of all his ways, first and last, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the book of the kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the city, <char style="add">[even]</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: but they brought him not into the sepulchres of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="29" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> began to reign <char style="add">[when he was]</char> five and twenty years old, and he reigned nine and twenty years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char>, the daughter of Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, according to all that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father had done.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />He in the first year of his reign, in the first month, opened the doors of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and repaired them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he brought in the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and gathered them together into the east street,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And said unto them, Hear me, you<char style="ord">2f</char> Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> now yourselves, and sanctify (make holy; set apart for God’s use) the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of your fathers, and carry forth the filthiness out of the holy <char style="add">[place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />For our fathers have trespassed, and done <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the eyes of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and have forsaken him, and have turned away their faces from the habitation of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and turned <char style="add">[their]</char> backs.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Also they have shut up the doors of the porch, and put out the lamps, and have not burned incense nor offered burnt offerings in the holy <char style="add">[place]</char> unto the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />For what reason the wrath of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was upon Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and he has delivered them to trouble, to astonishment, and to hissing, as you<char style="ord">2f</char> see with your eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For, lo, our fathers have fallen by the sword, and our sons and our daughters and our wives <char style="add">[are]</char> in captivity for this.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Now <char style="add">[it is]</char> in my heart to make a covenant with the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that his fierce wrath may turn away from us.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />My sons, be not now negligent: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has chosen you to stand before him, to serve him, and that you<char style="ord">2f</char> should minister unto him, and burn incense.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> arose, Machat <char style="add">[grasping]</char> the son of ‘Amasai <char style="add">[burdensome]</char>, and Yo’el <char style="add">[Yehovah is God]</char> the son of ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char>, of the sons of the K’hati: and of the sons of M’rari <char style="add">[Bitter]</char>, Kish <char style="add">[bent]</char> the son of ‘Abdi <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char>, and ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the son of Yehallel’el <char style="add">[God is praised]</char>: and of the Gershuni <char style="add">[Exiled Ones]</char>; Yo’ach <char style="add">[Yahovah is brother]</char> the son of Zimah <char style="add">[plotter]</char>, and ‘Eden <char style="add">[pleasure]</char> the son of Yo’ach <char style="add">[Yahovah is brother]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And of the sons of Elitzafan <char style="add">[My God has Protected]</char>; Shimri <char style="add">[vigilant]</char>, and Ye’i’el <char style="add">[God sweeps away]</char>: and of the sons of Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char>; Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char>, and Matanyah <char style="add">[gift of Yehovah]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And of the sons of Heiman <char style="add">[faithful]</char>; Jehiel, and Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char>: and of the sons of Y’dutun <char style="add">[praising]</char>; Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>, and Uzziel <char style="add">[My Strength is God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And they gathered their brethren, and sanctified themselves, and came, according to the commandment of the king, by the words of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to cleanse the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the priests went into the inner part of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to cleanse <char style="add">[it]</char>, and brought out all the uncleanness that they found in the temple of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> into the court of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> took <char style="add">[it]</char>, to carry <char style="add">[it]</char> out abroad into the brook Kidron <char style="add">[dark]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Now they began on the first <char style="add">[day]</char> of the first month to sanctify (make holy; set apart for God’s use), and on the eighth day of the month came they to the porch of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: so they sanctified the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in eight days; and in the sixteenth day of the first month they made an end.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then they went in to Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> the king, and said, We have cleansed all the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the altar of burnt offering, with all the vessels thereof, and the showbread table, with all the vessels thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Moreover all the vessels, which king Achaz <char style="add">[he has grasped]</char> in his reign did cast away in his transgression, have we prepared and sanctified, and, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> before the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> the king rose early, and gathered the rulers of the city, and went up to the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And they brought seven bullocks, and seven rams, and seven lambs, and seven he goats, for a sin offering for the kingdom, and for the sanctuary, and for Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>. And he commanded the priests the sons of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> to offer <char style="add">[them]</char> on the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />So they killed the bullocks, and the priests received the blood, and sprinkled <char style="add">[it]</char> on the altar: likewise, when they had killed the rams, they sprinkled the blood upon the altar: they killed also the lambs, and they sprinkled the blood upon the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And they brought forth the he goats <char style="add">[for]</char> the sin offering before the king and the congregation; and they laid their hands upon them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the priests killed them, and they made reconciliation with their blood upon the altar, to make an atonement for all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: for the king commanded <char style="add">[that]</char> the burnt offering and the sin offering <char style="add">[should be made]</char> for all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And he set the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with cymbals, with psalteries, and with harps, according to the commandment of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and of Gad <char style="add">[Good Fortune with Troublesome Effort]</char> the king’s seer, and Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet: for <char style="add">[so was]</char> the commandment of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> by his prophets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> stood with the instruments of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and the priests with the trumpets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> commanded to offer the burnt offering upon the altar. And when the burnt offering began, the song of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> began <char style="add">[also]</char> with the trumpets, and with the instruments <char style="add">[ordained]</char> by David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And all the congregation worshipped, and the singers sang, and the trumpeters sounded: <char style="add">[and]</char> all <char style="add">[this continued]</char> until the burnt offering was finished.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And when they had made an end of offering, the king and all that were present with him bowed themselves, and worshipped.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Moreover Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> the king and the princes commanded the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> to sing praise unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> with the words of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and of Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char> the seer. And they sang praises with gladness, and they bowed their heads and worshipped.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Then Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> answered and said, Now you<char style="ord">2f</char> have consecrated yourselves unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, come near and bring sacrifices and thank offerings into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And the congregation brought in sacrifices and thank offerings; and as many as were of a free heart burnt offerings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And the number of the burnt offerings, which the congregation brought, was threescore and ten bullocks, an hundred rams, <char style="add">[and]</char> two hundred lambs: all these <char style="add">[were]</char> for a burnt offering to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And the consecrated things <char style="add">[were]</char> six hundred oxen and three thousand sheep.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />But the priests were too few, so that they could not flay <char style="pn">(stip the skin off)</char> all the burnt offerings: wherefore their brethren the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> did help them, till the work was ended, and until the <char style="add">[other]</char> priests had sanctified themselves: for the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to] [were]</char> more upright in heart to sanctify (make holy; set apart for God’s use) themselves than the priests.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And also the burnt offerings <char style="add">[were]</char> in abundance, with the fat of the peace offerings, and the drink offerings for <char style="add">[every]</char> burnt offering. So the service of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was set in order.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> rejoiced, and all the people, that God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had prepared the people: for the thing was <char style="add">[done]</char> suddenly.</para>
  <chapter number="30" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> sent to all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and wrote letters also to Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> and M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, that they should come to the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, to keep the Passover unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For the king had taken counsel, and his princes, and all the congregation in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, to keep the Passover in the second month.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />For they could not keep it at that time, because the priests had not sanctified themselves sufficiently, neither had the people gathered themselves together to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the thing pleased the king and all the congregation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />So they established a decree to make proclamation throughout all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, from Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char> even to Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, that they should come to keep the Passover unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: for they had not done <char style="add">[it]</char> of a long <char style="add">[time in such sort]</char> as it was written.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So the posts went with the letters from the king and his princes throughout all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and according to the commandment of the king, saying, You<char style="ord">2f</char> people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, turn again unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, Yitz’khak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and he will return to the remnant of you, that are escaped out of the hand of the kings of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem [name] (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And be not you<char style="ord">2f</char> like your fathers, and like your brethren, which trespassed against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers, <char style="add">[who]</char> therefore gave them up to desolation, as you<char style="ord">2f</char> see.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Now be you<char style="ord">2f</char> not stiffnecked, as your fathers <char style="add">[were, but]</char> yield yourselves unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and enter into his sanctuary, which he has sanctified forever: and serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, that the fierceness of his wrath may turn away from you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For if you<char style="ord">2f</char> turn again unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, your brethren and your children <char style="add">[shall find]</char> compassion before them that lead them captive, so that they shall come again into this land: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [is]</char> gracious and merciful, and will not turn away <char style="add">[his]</char> face from you, if you<char style="ord">2f</char> return unto him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So the posts passed from city to city through the country of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> and M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> even unto Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char>: but they laughed them to scorn, and mocked them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Nevertheless diverse of Asher <char style="add">[Happy]</char> and M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> and of Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char> humbled themselves, and came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Also in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> the hand of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> was to give them one heart to do the commandment of the king and of the princes, by the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And there assembled at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> much people to keep the feast of unleavened bread in the second month, a very great congregation.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And they arose and took away the altars that <char style="add">[were]</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and all the altars for incense took they away, and cast <char style="add">[them]</char> into the brook Kidron <char style="add">[dark]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then they killed the Passover on the fourteenth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the second month: and the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> were ashamed, and sanctified themselves, and brought in the burnt offerings into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And they stood in their place after their manner, according to the law of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: the priests sprinkled the blood, <char style="add">[which they received]</char> of the hand of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />For <char style="add">[there were]</char> many in the congregation that were not sanctified: therefore the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> had the charge of the killing of the passovers for every one <char style="add">[that was]</char> not clean, to sanctify (make holy; set apart for God’s use) <char style="add">[them]</char> unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />For a multitude of the people, <char style="add">[even]</char> many of Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, Yissakhar <char style="add">[There Is Recompense]</char>, and Z’vulun <char style="add">[Glorious Dwelling Place]</char>, had not cleansed themselves, yet did they eat the Passover otherwise than it was written. But Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> prayed for them, saying, The good LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> pardon every one</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[That]</char> prepares his heart to seek God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of his fathers, though <char style="add">[he be]</char> not <char style="add">[cleansed]</char> according to the purification of the sanctuary.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> listened to Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, and healed the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that were present at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> kept the feast of unleavened bread seven days with great gladness: and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> and the priests praised the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> day by day, <char style="add">[singing]</char> with loud instruments unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> spoke comfortably unto all the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> that taught the good knowledge of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and they did eat throughout the feast seven days, offering peace offerings, and making confession to the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the whole assembly took counsel to keep other seven days: and they kept <char style="add">[other]</char> seven days with gladness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />For Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> did give to the congregation a thousand bullocks and seven thousand sheep; and the princes gave to the congregation a thousand bullocks and ten thousand sheep: and a great number of priests sanctified themselves.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And all the congregation of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, with the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and all the congregation that came out of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and the strangers that came out of the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and that dwelt in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, rejoiced.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />So there was great joy in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: for since the time of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> the son of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [there was]</char> not the like in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Then the priests the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> arose and Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> the people: and their voice was heard, and their prayer came <char style="add">[up]</char> to his holy dwelling place, <char style="add">[even]</char> unto heaven.</para>
  <chapter number="31" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now when all this was finished, all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that were present went out to the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and broke the images in pieces, and cut down the groves, and threw down the high places and the altars out of all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, in Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char> also and M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, until they had utterly destroyed them all. Then all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> returned, every man to his possession, into their own cities.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> appointed the courses of the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> after their courses, every man according to his service, the priests and Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> for burnt offerings and for peace offerings, to minister, and to give thanks, and to praise in the gates of the tents of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[He appointed]</char> also the king’s portion of his substance for the burnt offerings, <char style="add">[that is to say]</char>, for the morning and evening burnt offerings, and the burnt offerings for the Shabbat, and for the new moons, and for the set feasts, as <char style="add">[it is]</char> written in the law of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Moreover he commanded the people that dwelt in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to give the portion of the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, that they might be encouraged in the law of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And as soon as the commandment came abroad, the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> brought in abundance the firstfruits of corn, wine, and oil, and honey, and of all the increase of the field; and the tithe of all <char style="add">[things]</char> brought they in abundantly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And <char style="add">[concerning]</char> the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, that dwelt in the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, they also brought in the tithe of oxen and sheep, and the tithe of holy things which were consecrated unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and laid <char style="add">[them]</char> by heaps.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />In the third month they began to lay the foundation of the heaps, and finished <char style="add">[them]</char> in the seventh month.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And when Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> and the princes came and saw the heaps, they Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and his people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> questioned with the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> concerning the heaps.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the chief priest of the house of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> answered him, and said, Since <char style="add">[the people]</char> began to bring the offerings into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, we have had enough to eat, and have left plenty: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> his people; and that which is left <char style="add">[is]</char> this great store.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Then Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> commanded to prepare chambers in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and they prepared <char style="add">[them]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And brought in the offerings and the tithes and the dedicated <char style="add">[things]</char> faithfully: over which Konanyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has established]</char> the Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to] [was]</char> ruler, and Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> his brother <char style="add">[was]</char> the next.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Jehiel, and ‘Azazyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is mighty]</char>, and Nachat <char style="add">[rest]</char>, and ‘Asah’el <char style="add">[God-made]</char>, and Yerimot <char style="add">[He is Most High]</char>, and Yozavad <char style="add">[Yehovah has endowed]</char>, and Eli’el <char style="add">[my God is God]</char>, and Yishmachyah <char style="add">[Yehovah sustains]</char>, and Machat <char style="add">[grasping]</char>, and B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char>, <char style="add">[were]</char> overseers under the hand of Konanyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has established]</char> and Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> his brother, at the commandment of Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> the king, and ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the ruler of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Kore <char style="add">[crier]</char> the son of Yimnah <char style="add">[right hand]</char> the Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, the porter toward the east, <char style="add">[was]</char> over the freewill offerings of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, to distribute the oblations of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the most holy things.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And next him <char style="add">[were]</char> ‘Eden <char style="add">[pleasure]</char>, and Minyamin <char style="add">[from the right hand]</char>, and Yeshua <char style="add">[he is saved]</char>, and Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char>, Amaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah speaks]</char>, and Sh’khanyahu <char style="add">[dweller with Yehovah]</char>, in the cities of the priests, in <char style="add">[their]</char> set office, to give to their brethren by courses, as well to the great as to the small:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Beside their genealogy of males, from three years old and upward, <char style="add">[even]</char> unto every one that enters into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, his daily portion for their service in their charges according to their courses;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Both to the genealogy of the priests by the house of their fathers, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> from twenty years old and upward, in their charges by their courses;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And to the genealogy of all their little ones, their wives, and their sons, and their daughters, through all the congregation: for in their set office they sanctified themselves in holiness:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Also of the sons of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char> the priests, <char style="add">[which were]</char> in the fields of the suburbs of their cities, in every single <char style="pn">(each one separately)</char> city, the men that were expressed by name, to give portions to all the males among the priests, and to all that were reckoned by genealogies among the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And thus did Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> throughout all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and wrought <char style="add">[that which was]</char> good and right and tbefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And in every work that he began in the service of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and in the law, and in the commandments, to seek his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, he did <char style="add">[it]</char> with all his heart, and prospered.</para>
  <chapter number="32" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />After these things, and the establishment thereof, Sancheriv [Sin <char style="pn">(the moon)</char> multiplied brothers] king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem [name] (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> came, and entered into Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and encamped against the fenced cities, and thought to win them for himself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And when Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> saw that Sancheriv <char style="add">[Sin (the moon) multiplied brothers]</char> was come, and that he was purposed to fight against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />He took counsel with his princes and his mighty men to stop the waters of the fountains which <char style="add">[were]</char> without the city: and they did help him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />So there was gathered much people together, who stopped all the fountains, and the brook that ran through the midst of the land, saying, Why should the kings of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem [name] (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> come, and find much water?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Also he strengthened himself, and built up all the wall that was broken, and raised <char style="add">[it]</char> up to the towers, and another wall without, and repaired Millo <char style="add">[fortification (defensive structure) or mound] [in]</char> the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and made darts and shields in abundance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he set captains of war over the people, and gathered them together to him in the street of the gate of the city, and spoke comfortably to them, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Be strong and courageous, be not afraid nor dismayed for the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem [name] (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, nor for all the multitude that <char style="add">[is]</char> with him: for <char style="add">[there be]</char> more with us than with him:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />With him <char style="add">[is]</char> an arm of flesh; but with us <char style="add">[is]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> to help us, and to fight our battles. And the people rested themselves upon the words of Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />After this did Sancheriv <char style="add">[Sin (the moon) multiplied brothers]</char> king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem [name] (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char> send his servants to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, <char style="pn">(but he [himself laid siege] against Lakhish [Invincible], and all his power with him,)</char> unto Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and unto all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> that <char style="add">[were]</char> at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Thus says Sancheriv [Sin <char style="pn">(the moon)</char> multiplied brothers] king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> (the land of the sons of Shem <char style="add">[name]</char> <char style="pn">(name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, Whereon do you<char style="ord">2f</char> trust, that you<char style="ord">2f</char> abide in the siege in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Does not Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> persuade you to give over yourselves to die by famine and by thirst, saying, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> shall deliver us out of the hand of the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem [name] (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Has not the same Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> taken away his high places and his altars, and commanded Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, saying, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall worship before one altar, and burn incense upon it?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Know you<char style="ord">2f</char> not what I and my fathers have done unto all the people of <char style="add">[other]</char> lands? were the gods of the nations of those lands any ways able to deliver their lands out of my hand?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Who <char style="add">[was there]</char> among all the gods of those nations that my fathers utterly destroyed, that could deliver his people out of my hand, that your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> should be able to deliver you out of my hand?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Now therefore let not Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> deceive you, nor persuade you on this manner, neither yet believe him: for no god of any nation or kingdom was able to deliver his people out of my hand, and out of the hand of my fathers: how much less shall your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> deliver you out of my hand?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And his servants spoke yet <char style="add">[more]</char> against the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and against his servant Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />He wrote also letters to rail on the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and to speak against him, saying, As the gods of the nations of <char style="add">[other]</char> lands have not delivered their people out of my hand, so shall not the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> deliver his people out of my hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then they cried with a loud voice in the Y’hudit <char style="pn">(Y’hudim (Judeans)’)</char> speech unto the people of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> that <char style="add">[were]</char> on the wall, to affright them, and to trouble them; that they might take the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And they spoke against the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, as against the gods of the people of the earth, <char style="add">[which were]</char> the work of the hands of man.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And for this <char style="add">[cause]</char> Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> the king, and the prophet Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> the son of Amotz <char style="add">[strong]</char>, prayed and cried to heaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sent an angel, which cut off all the mighty men of valour, and the leaders and captains in the camp of the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem [name] (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>. So he returned with shame of face to his own land. And when he was come into the house of his god, they that came forth of his own bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char> killed him there with the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Thus the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> saved Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> and the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> from the hand of Sancheriv <char style="add">[Sin (the moon) multiplied brothers]</char> the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem [name] (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, and from the hand of all <char style="add">[other]</char>, and guided them on every side.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And many brought gifts unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and presents to Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: so that he was magnified in the sight of all nations from thenceforth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />In those days Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> was sick to the death, and prayed unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and he spoke unto him, and he gave him a sign.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> rendered not again according to the benefit <char style="add">[done]</char> unto him; for his heart was lifted up: therefore there was wrath upon him, and upon Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Yet Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> humbled himself for the pride of his heart, <char style="add">[both]</char> he and the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, so that the wrath of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came not upon them in the days of Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> had exceeding much riches and honour: and he made himself treasuries for silver, and for gold, and for precious stones, and for spices, and for shields, and for all manner of pleasant jewels;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Storehouses also for the increase of corn, and wine, and oil; and stalls for all manner of beasts, and stables for flocks.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Moreover he provided him cities, and possessions of flocks and herds in abundance: for God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had given him substance very much.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />This same Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> also stopped the upper watercourse of Gikhon <char style="pn">(Bursting Forth)</char>, and brought it straight down to the west side of the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>. And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> prospered in all his works.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />However in <char style="add">[the business of]</char> the ambassadors of the princes of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, who sent unto him to enquire of the wonder that was <char style="add">[done]</char> in the land, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> left him, to try him, that he might know all <char style="add">[that was]</char> in his heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char>, and his goodness, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the vision of Yesha’yahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has saved]</char> the prophet, the son of Amotz <char style="add">[strong]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> in the book of the kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the most important of the sepulchres of the sons of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> did him honour at his death. And M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="33" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget] [was]</char> twelve years old when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty and five years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />But did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, like unto the abominations of the heathen, whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had cast out before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />For he built again the high places which Hizkiyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah is my strength]</char> his father had broken down, and he reared up altars for Ba’alim <char style="add">[lords (false gods)]</char>, and made groves, and worshipped all the army of heaven, and served them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Also he built altars in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, whereof the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had said, In Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> shall my name be forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he built altars for all the army of heaven in the two courts of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he caused his children to pass through the fire in the valley of the son of Hinnom <char style="add">[Lamentation]</char>: also he observed times, and used enchantments, and used witchcraft, and dealt with a familiar spirit, and with wizards: he wrought much evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to provoke him to anger.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he set a carved image, the idol which he had made, in the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, of which God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had said to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> and to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> his son, In this house, and in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, which I have chosen before all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, will I put my name forever:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Neither will I any more remove the foot of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from out of the land which I have appointed for your fathers; so that they will take heed to do all that I have commanded them, according to the whole law and the statutes and the ordinances by the hand of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />So M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> made Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to err, <char style="add">[and]</char> to do worse than the heathen, whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had destroyed before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke to M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, and to his people: but they would not hearken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For what reason the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> brought upon them the captains of the host of the king of Ashur <char style="add">[the level plain]</char> <char style="pn">(the land of the sons of Shem [name] (name, renown (great reputation; being well-known)))</char>, which took M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> among the thorns, and bound him with fetters, and carried him to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And when he was in affliction, he besought the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and humbled himself greatly before the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of his fathers,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And prayed unto him: and he was intreated of him, and heard his supplication, and brought him again to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> into his kingdom. Then M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> knew that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> he <char style="add">[was]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Now after this he built a wall without the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, on the west side of Gikhon <char style="pn">(Bursting Forth)</char>, in the valley, even to the entering in at the fish gate, and compassed about ‘Ofel <char style="add">[hill]</char>, and raised it up a very great height, and put captains of war in all the fenced cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he took away the strange gods, and the idol out of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and all the altars that he had built in the mount of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and cast <char style="add">[them]</char> out of the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he repaired the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and sacrificed thereon peace offerings and thank offerings, and commanded Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> to serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Nevertheless the people did sacrifice still in the high places, <char style="add">[yet]</char> unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> only.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, and his prayer unto his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and the words of the seers that spoke to him in the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, behold, they <char style="add">[are written]</char> in the book of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />His prayer also, and <char style="add">[how God-Elōhīm (The Living Word) [The Many Powered]]</char> was intreated of him, and all his sin, and his trespass, and the places wherein he built high places, and set up groves and graven images, before he was humbled: behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written among the sayings of the seers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />So M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> slept with his fathers, and they buried him in his own house: and ‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman] [was]</char> two and twenty years old when he began to reign, and reigned two years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as did M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> his father: for ‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman]</char> sacrificed unto all the carved images which M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> his father had made, and served them;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And humbled not himself before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> his father had humbled himself; but ‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman]</char> trespassed more and more.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And his servants conspired against him, and killed him in his own house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But the people of the land killed all them that had conspired against king ‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman]</char>; and the people of the land made Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> his son king in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="34" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals] [was]</char> eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> one and thirty years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and walked in the ways of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father, and declined <char style="add">[neither]</char> to the right hand, nor to the left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />For in the eighth year of his reign, while he was yet young, he began to seek after the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father: and in the twelfth year he began to purge Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> from the high places, and the groves, and the carved images, and the molten images.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And they broke down the altars of Ba’alim <char style="add">[lords (false gods)]</char> in his presence; and the images, that <char style="add">[were]</char> on high above them, he cut down; and the groves, and the carved images, and the molten images, he broke in pieces, and made dust <char style="add">[of them]</char>, and strewed <char style="add">[it]</char> upon the graves of them that had sacrificed unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he burnt the bones of the priests upon their altars, and cleansed Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And <char style="add">[so did he]</char> in the cities of M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, and Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and Shim’on <char style="add">[he who hears]</char>, even unto Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>, with their mattocks round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And when he had broken down the altars and the groves, and had beaten the graven images into powder, and cut down all the idols throughout all the land of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, he returned to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Now in the eighteenth year of his reign, when he had purged the land, and the house, he sent Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> the son of Atzalyahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has set apart]</char>, and Ma’aseiyah <char style="add">[work of Yehovah]</char> the governor of the city, and Yo’ach <char style="add">[Yahovah is brother]</char> the son of Yo’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has grasped]</char> the recorder, to repair the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And when they came to Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> the High Priest, they delivered the money that was brought into the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> that kept the doors had gathered of the hand of M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char> and Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and of all the remnant of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and of all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>; and they returned to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And they put <char style="add">[it]</char> in the hand of the workmen that had the oversight of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and they gave it to the workmen that wrought in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to repair and amend the house:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Even to the artificers and builders gave they <char style="add">[it]</char>, to buy cut stone, and timber for couplings, and to floor the houses which the kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> had destroyed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the men did the work faithfully: and the overseers of them <char style="add">[were]</char> Yachat <char style="add">[He will snatch up]</char> and ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char>, the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, of the sons of M’rari <char style="add">[Bitter]</char>; and Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char> and Meshulam <char style="add">[friend]</char>, of the sons of the K’hati, to set <char style="add">[it]</char> forward; and <char style="add">[other of]</char> the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, all that could skill of instruments of music.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Also <char style="add">[they were]</char> over the bearers of burdens, and <char style="add">[were]</char> overseers of all that wrought the work in any manner of service: and of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to] [there were]</char> scribes, and officers, and porters.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And when they brought out the money that was brought into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> the priest found a book of the law of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[given]</char> by Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> answered and said to Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> the scribe, I have found the book of the law in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> delivered the book to Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> carried the book to the king, and brought the king word back again, saying, All that was committed to you<char style="ord">i</char> servants, they do <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And they have gathered together the money that was found in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and have delivered it into the hand of the overseers, and to the hand of the workmen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> the scribe told the king, saying, Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> the priest has given me a book. And Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> read it before the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the king had heard the words of the law, that he rent his clothes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the king commanded Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char>, and Achikam <char style="add">[my brother has arisen]</char> the son of Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char>, and Avdon <char style="add">[Servile]</char> the son of Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[Who is Like God?]</char>, and Shafan <char style="add">[coney]</char> the scribe, and ‘Asayah <char style="add">[made by Yehovah]</char> a servant of the king’s, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Go, enquire of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> for me, and for them that are left in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, concerning the words of the book that is found: for great <char style="add">[is]</char> the wrath of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> that is poured out upon us, because our fathers have not kept the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to do after all that is written in this book.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char>, and <char style="add">[they]</char> that the king <char style="add">[had appointed]</char>, went to Huldah <char style="add">[weasel]</char> the prophetess, the wife of Shalum <char style="add">[retribution]</char> the son of Tikevah <char style="add">[hope]</char>, the son of Hasrat <char style="add">[lack]</char>, keeper of the wardrobe; (now she dwelt in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> in the college) and they spoke to her to that <char style="add">[effect]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And she answered them, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Tell you<char style="ord">2f</char> the man that sent you to me,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Behold, I will bring evil upon this place, and upon the inhabitants thereof, <char style="add">[even]</char> all the curses that are written in the book which they have read before the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Because they have forsaken me, and have burned incense unto other gods, that they might provoke me to anger with all the works of their hands; therefore my wrath shall be poured out upon this place, and shall not be quenched.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And as for the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, who sent you to enquire of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, so shall you<char style="ord">2f</char> say unto him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [concerning]</char> the words which you<char style="ord">i</char> have heard;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Because your<char style="ord">i</char> heart was tender, and you<char style="ord">i</char> did humble yourself before God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, when you<char style="ord">i</char> heard his words against this place, and against the inhabitants thereof, and humbled yourself before me, and did rend <char style="pn">(tear apart; forcefully rip apart)</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> clothes, and weep before me; I have even heard <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> also, says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Behold, I will gather you<char style="ord">i</char> to your<char style="ord">i</char> fathers, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall be gathered to your<char style="ord">i</char> grave in peace, neither shall your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes see all the evil that I will bring upon this place, and upon the inhabitants of the same. So they brought the king word again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Then the king sent and gathered together all the elders of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the king went up into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and all the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and the priests, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and all the people, great and small: and he read in their ears all the words of the book of the covenant that was found in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the king stood in his place, and made a covenant before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, to walk after the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and to keep his commandments, and his testimonies, and his statutes, with all his heart, and with all his soul, to perform the words of the covenant which are written in this book.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And he caused all that were present in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char> to stand <char style="add">[to it]</char>. And the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> did according to the covenant of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> took away all the abominations out of all the countries that <char style="add">[pertained]</char> to the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and made all that were present in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to serve, <char style="add">[even]</char> to serve the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. <char style="add">[And]</char> all his days they departed not from following the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers.</para>
  <chapter number="35" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Moreover Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> kept a Passover unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: and they killed the Passover on the fourteenth <char style="add">[day]</char> of the first month.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he set the priests in their charges, and encouraged them to the service of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And said unto the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> that taught all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which were holy unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Put <char style="add">[a bow]</char> the holy ark in the house which Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> the son of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did build; <char style="add">[it shall]</char> not <char style="add">[be]</char> a burden upon <char style="add">[your]</char> shoulders: serve now the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and his people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And prepare <char style="add">[yourselves]</char> by the houses of your fathers, after your courses, according to the writing of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and according to the writing of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> his son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And stand in the holy <char style="add">[place]</char> according to the divisions of the families of the fathers of your brethren the people, and <char style="add">[after]</char> the division of the families of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So kill the Passover, and sanctify <char style="pn">(make holy; set apart for God’s use)</char> yourselves, and prepare your brethren, that <char style="add">[they]</char> may do according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> by the hand of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> gave to the people, of the flock, lambs and kids, all for the Passover offerings, for all that were present, to the number of thirty thousand, and three thousand bullocks: these <char style="add">[were]</char> of the king’s substance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And his princes gave willingly unto the people, to the priests, and to the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>: Hilkiyahu <char style="add">[my portion is Yehovah]</char> and Z’kharyah <char style="add">[Yehovah remembers]</char> and Jehiel, rulers of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, gave unto the priests for the Passover offerings two thousand and six hundred <char style="add">[small cattle]</char>, and three hundred oxen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Konanyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has established]</char> also, and Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char> and N’tan’el <char style="add">[God’s Gift]</char>, his brethren, and Hashavyah <char style="add">[Yehovah has considered]</char> and Ye’i’el <char style="add">[God sweeps away]</char> and Yozavad <char style="add">[Yehovah has endowed]</char>, chief of the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, gave unto the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> for Passover offerings five thousand <char style="add">[small cattle]</char>, and five hundred oxen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So the service was prepared, and the priests stood in their place, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> in their courses, according to the king’s commandment.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And they killed the Passover, and the priests sprinkled <char style="add">[the blood]</char> from their hands, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> flayed <char style="add">[them]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And they removed the burnt offerings, that they might give according to the divisions of the families of the people, to offer unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as <char style="add">[it is]</char> written in the book of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>. And so <char style="add">[did they]</char> with the oxen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And they roasted the Passover with fire according to the ordinance: but the <char style="add">[other]</char> holy <char style="add">[offerings]</char> coocked <char style="pn">(boiled)</char> they in pots, and in caldrons, and in pans, and divided <char style="add">[them]</char> speedily among all the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And afterward they made ready for themselves, and for the priests: because the priests the sons of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High] [were busied]</char> in offering of burnt offerings and the fat until night; therefore the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> prepared for themselves, and for the priests the sons of Aharon <char style="add">[Bright, Very High]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the singers the sons of Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer] [were]</char> in their place, according to the commandment of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and Asaf <char style="add">[gatherer]</char>, and Heiman <char style="add">[faithful]</char>, and Y’dutun <char style="add">[praising]</char> the king’s seer; and the porters <char style="add">[waited]</char> at every gate; they might not depart from their service; for their brethren the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> prepared for them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />So all the service of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was prepared the same day, to keep the Passover, and to offer burnt offerings upon the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, according to the commandment of king Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that were present kept the Passover at that time, and the feast of unleavened bread seven days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And there was no Passover like to that kept in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> from the days of Sh’mu’el <char style="add">[His name is El]</char> the prophet; neither did all the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> keep such a Passover as Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> kept, and the priests, and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char>, and all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that were present, and the inhabitants of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />In the eighteenth year of the reign of Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> was this Passover kept.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />After all this, when Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> had prepared the temple, N’kho <char style="add">[lame]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> came up to fight against Kark’mish <char style="add">[fortress of Chemosh (subdue)]</char> by Euphrates <char style="pn">(to break forth, to gush)</char>: and Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> went out against him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />But he sent ambassadors to him, saying, What have I to do with you<char style="ord">i</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>? <char style="add">[I come]</char> not against you<char style="ord">i</char> this day, but against the house which I have war: for God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> commanded me to make haste: refrain <char style="pn">(restrain; refrein from acting)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> from <char style="add">[meddling with]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, who <char style="add">[is]</char> with me, that he destroy you<char style="ord">i</char> not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Nevertheless Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> would not turn his face from him, but disguised himself, that he might fight with him, and listened not unto the words of N’kho <char style="add">[lame]</char> from the mouth of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and came to fight in the valley of Megiddo <char style="add">[Place of Crowds]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the archers shot at king Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char>; and the king said to his servants, Have me away; for I am sore wounded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />His servants therefore took him out of that chariot, and put him in the second chariot that he had; and they brought him to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and he died, and was buried in <char style="add">[one of]</char> the sepulchres of his fathers. And all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> mourned for Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Yirmeyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah has appointed]</char> lamented for Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char>: and all the singing men and the singing women spoke of Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> in their lamentations to this day, and made them an ordinance in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the lamentations.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char>, and his goodness, according to <char style="add">[that which was]</char> written in the law of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And his deeds, first and last, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the book of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="36" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then the people of the land took Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> the son of Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char>, and made him king in his father’s stead in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized] [was]</char> twenty and three years old when he began to reign, and he reigned three months in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> put him down at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and condemned the land in an hundred talents of silver and a talent <char style="pn">(weight of money; weight; gift)</char> of gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> made Elyakim <char style="add">[God sets up]</char> his brother king over Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and turned his name to Y’hoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char>. And N’kho <char style="add">[lame]</char> took Y’ho’achaz <char style="add">[Yehovah has seized]</char> his brother, and carried him to Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Y’hoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up] [was]</char> twenty and five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: and he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Against him came up N’vukhadnetzar <char style="add">[May Nebo protect the crown]</char> king of Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, and bound him in fetters, to carry him to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />N’vukhadnetzar <char style="add">[May Nebo protect the crown]</char> also carried of the vessels of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, and put them in his temple at Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Y’hoyakim <char style="add">[Yehovah raises up]</char>, and his abominations which he did, and that which was found in him, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the book of the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>: and Y’hoyakhin <char style="add">[Yehovah establishes]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Y’hoyakhin <char style="add">[Yehovah establishes] [was]</char> eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned three months and ten days in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: and he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And when the year was expired, king N’vukhadnetzar <char style="add">[May Nebo protect the crown]</char> sent, and brought him to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>, with the goodly vessels of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and made Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char> his brother king over Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous] [was]</char> one and twenty years old when he began to reign, and reigned eleven years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> humbled not himself before Yirmeyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah has appointed]</char> the prophet <char style="add">[speaking]</char> from the mouth of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he also rebelled against king N’vukhadnetzar <char style="add">[May Nebo protect the crown]</char>, who had made him swear by God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>: but he stiffened his neck, and hardened his heart from turning unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Moreover all the chief of the priests, and the people, transgressed very much after all the abominations of the heathen; and polluted the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> which he had consecrated in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of their fathers sent to them by his messengers, rising up early, and sending; because he had compassion on his people, and on his dwelling place:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />But they mocked the messengers of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and despised his words, and misused his prophets, until the wrath of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> arose against his people, till <char style="add">[there was]</char> no remedy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Therefore he brought upon them the king of the Kasdim <char style="add">[clod-breakers] [clod-breakers]</char>, who killed their young men with the sword in the house of their sanctuary, and had no compassion upon young man or virgin, old man, or him that stooped for age: he gave <char style="add">[them]</char> all into his hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And all the vessels of the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, great and small, and the treasures of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the treasures of the king, and of his princes; all <char style="add">[these]</char> he brought to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And they burnt the house of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and broke down the wall of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and burnt all the palaces thereof with fire, and destroyed all the goodly vessels thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And them that had escaped from the sword carried he away to Bavel <char style="pn">(to jumble, or a confused medley of sounds; confusion; gate of the deity)</char> <char style="pn">(Babylon)</char> <char style="add">[confusion]</char>; where they were servants to him and his sons until the reign of the kingdom of Paras <char style="pn">(Persia)</char> <char style="add">[pure or splendid]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />To fulfil the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> by the mouth of Yirmeyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah has appointed]</char>, until the land had enjoyed her Shabbat: <char style="add">[for]</char> as long as she lay desolate she kept Shabbat <char style="add">[Rest]</char>, to fulfil threescore and ten years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Now in the first year of Koresh <char style="pn">(Cyrus)</char> <char style="add">[possess you the furnace]</char> king of Paras <char style="pn">(Persia)</char> <char style="add">[pure or splendid]</char>, that the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[spoken]</char> by the mouth of Yirmeyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah has appointed]</char> might be accomplished, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> stirred up the spirit of Koresh <char style="pn">(Cyrus)</char> <char style="add">[possess you the furnace]</char> king of Paras <char style="pn">(Persia)</char> <char style="add">[pure or splendid]</char>, that he made a proclamation throughout all his kingdom, and <char style="add">[put it]</char> also in writing, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Thus says Koresh <char style="pn">(Cyrus)</char> <char style="add">[possess you the furnace]</char> king of Paras <char style="pn">(Persia)</char> <char style="add">[pure or splendid]</char>, All the kingdoms of the earth has the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of heaven given me; and he has charged me to build him an house in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>. Who <char style="add">[is there]</char> among you of all his people? The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [be]</char> with him, and let him go up.</para>
</usx>